[Term]
id: CL:0000972
name: class switched memory B cell
namespace: cell
def: "A class switched memory B cell is a memory B cell that has undergone Ig class switching and therefore is IgM-negative on the cell surface. These cells are usually CD27-positive and have either IgG, IgE, or IgA on the cell surface." [GO_REF:0000031, GOC:dsd, GOC:rhs, ISBN:0781765196, PMID:20933013]
comment: Class switched memory B cells are also reportedly CD48-positive, CD229-positive, and CD352-positive.
