[Term]
id: UBERON:0000037
name: tertiary ovarian follicle
namespace: uberon
def: "A follicle that has reached the most mature stage of folliculogenesis, characterized by the presence of the antrum" [http://www.repropedia.org/antral-follicle, UBERON:cjm]
def: "Ovarian follicle is the basic unit of female reproductive biology and is composed of roughly spherical aggregations of cells found in the ovary. They contain a single oocyte (aka ovum or egg). These structures are periodically initiated to grow and develop, culminating in ovulation of usually a single competent oocyte. These eggs/ova are only developed once every menstrual cycle (i. e, once a month). [WP,unvetted]." [Wikipedia:Graafian_follicle]
