[Term]
id: UBERON:0000052
name: fornix of brain
namespace: uberon
def: "A C-shaped bundle of fibres (axons) in the brain, and carries signals from the hippocampus to the mammillary bodies and septal nuclei. It is typically divided into the columns (crus), body, commissure and the pre-commissural and post-commissural fornix (MM)." [NIFSTD:birnlex_705]
def: "The fornix (Latin, 'vault' or 'arch') is a C-shaped bundle of fibres in the brain, and carries signals from the hippocampus to the mammillary bodies and septal nuclei. [WP,unvetted]." [Wikipedia:Vaginal_fornix_of_brain_of_brain]
