[Term]
id: UBERON:0000100
name: blastopore
namespace: uberon
def: "Structure around the opening into the archenteron during the embryonic stages of an organism. The distinction between protostomes and deuterostomes is based on the direction in which the mouth (stoma) develops in relation to the blastopore." [Wikipedia:Blastopore]
def: "the orifice of invagination of the endomesodermal cells during the embryonic stages of an organism." [BGEE:ANN, http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/23103190, https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/660]
comment: In protostome development, the first opening in development, the blastopore, becomes the animal's mouth; In deuterostome development, the blastopore becomes the animal's anus
subset: early_development
subset: metazoa_core
