[Term]
id: UBERON:0000130
name: transverse foramen
namespace: uberon
def: "Foramen that pierces the transverse processes of the seven cervical vertebrae. In the upper six vertebrae, the foramen gives passage to the vertebral artery, vertebral vein, and a plexus of sympathetic nerves. The seventh foramen lacks the artery, but contains the vein and sympathetic nerves." [Wikipedia:Transverse_foramen]
