[Term]
id: UBERON:0000152
name: pelvic fin
namespace: uberon
def: "Paired fin located in the abdominal position of the body." [TAO:curator, VSAO:0000129]
def: "The paired pelvic or ventral fins are located ventrally below the pectoral fins. They are homologous to the hindlimbs of tetrapods. The pelvic fin assists the fish in going up or down through the water, turning sharply, and stopping quickly." [Wikipedia:Pectoral_fin#Fins]
comment: check definition of limb such that is excludes fins. Note the GO includes pectoral and pelvic fins as types of limbs.
