[Term]
id: UBERON:0000155
name: theca cell layer
namespace: uberon
def: "A layer of the ovarian follicle that consists of theca cells." [UBERON:cjm]
def: "A layer of the ovarian follicles. They appear as the follicles become tertiary follicles. The theca folliculi are responsible for the production of testosterone from androstenedione in females, and indirectly the production of estrogens by supplying the neighboring granulosa cells with androstenedione that can then be used as a substrate for aromatase." [Wikipedia:Theca_of_follicle]
