[Term]
id: UBERON:0000175
name: pleural effusion
namespace: uberon
def: "Pleural effusion is a bodily fluid that is produced in exess and accumulates in the pleural cavity, the fluid-filled space that surrounds the lungs. Excessive amounts of such fluid can impair breathing by limiting the expansion of the lungs during inhalation." [ENVO:02000033]
