[Term]
id: UBERON:0001139
name: common iliac vein
namespace: uberon
def: "A vein that drains the pelvis and lower limbs into the inferior vena cava." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_iliac_vein, MURDOCH:403]
def: "In human anatomy, the common iliac veins are formed by the external iliac veins and internal iliac veins and together, in the abdomen at the level of the fifth lumbar vertebrae, form the inferior vena cava. They drain blood from the pelvis and lower limbs. Both common iliac veins are accompanied along their course by common iliac arteries. [WP,unvetted]." [Wikipedia:Common_iliac_vein]
