[Term]
id: UBERON:0001174
name: common bile duct
namespace: uberon
def: "a tube-like anatomic structure in the human gastrointestinal tract. It is formed by the union of the common hepatic duct and the cystic duct (from the gall bladder). It is later joined by the pancreatic duct to form the ampulla of Vater. There, the two ducts are surrounded by the muscular sphincter of Oddi." [Wikipedia:Common_bile_duct]
def: "the part of the biliary tree formed by the union of the cystic duct and the common hepatic duct" [MP:0009495\,MGI\:csmith]
