[Term]
id: UBERON:0001213
name: intestinal villus
namespace: uberon
alt_id: UBERON:0007607
def: "the tiny hair-like projections that protrude from the inside of the small intestine that contain blood vessels that capture digested nutrients that are absorbed through the intestinal wall; the villi increase the absorptive surface area of the small intestine by approximately 30-fold" [MP:0008108\,MGI\:csmith\,MGI\:rbabiuk]
def: "Tiny, finger-like projections that protrude from the epithelial lining of the intestinal wall[WP]" [Wikipedia:Intestinal_villus]
comment: Editor notes: in mammals, villi are (largely?) absent from the large intestine, so we treat this as equivalent to small intestinal villus. small/large subdivision may not make sense for all speciesi for which this is present (see ZFA). Note that VHOG quotes ISBN:978-0030223693 as suggesting there are some villi in the large intestine.  AO Notes: the BTO class refers to a generic villous
