[Term]
id: UBERON:0001227
name: minor calyx
namespace: uberon
def: "portion of the urinary collecting system within the kidney that drains one renal papilla" [http://anatomy.uams.edu/anatomyhtml/kidney.html]
def: "The minor calyx, in the kidney, surrounds the apex of the malpighian pyramids. Urine formed in the kidney passes through a papilla at the apex into the minor calyx then into the major calyx. Peristalsis of the smooth muscle originating in pace-maker cells originating in the walls of the calyces propels urine through the pelvis and ureters to the bladder. [WP,unvetted]." [Wikipedia:Minor_calyx]
comment: one renal papilla projects into the lumen of one minor calyx; several minor calyces unite to form a major calyx
comment: This class was created automatically from a combination of ontologies
