[Term]
id: UBERON:0001235
name: adrenal cortex
namespace: uberon
def: "Situated along the perimeter of the adrenal gland, the adrenal cortex mediates the stress response through the production of mineralocorticoids and glucocorticoids, including aldosterone and cortisol respectively. It is also a secondary site of androgen synthesis. [WP,unvetted]." [Wikipedia:Adrenal_cortex]
def: "the thick outer layer of the adrenal gland that produces and secretes steroid hormones such as corticosterone, estrone and aldosterone" [MP:0008288\,ISBN\:0-683-40008-8\,MGI\:llw2]
comment: Taxon notes: Kardong states that mammals are the first to have distinct cortext and medulla, but this contradicts XAO
