property_value: external_definition "Cavity for the articulation of the proximal bone of the hind limb.[AAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-06-20", external_class="AAO:0000770", ontology="AAO", source="AAO:LAP"}
property_value: external_ontology_notes "whilst WP defines this as a surface, MA treats it as a bone. There are other FMA classes that may be better suited to representing the surface. " xsd:string {external_ontology="MA"}
property_value: homology_notes "During the transformation from the osteolepiform fins to tetrapod limbs, the appendages and girdles underwent a number of radical changes. The pelvic girdle became a weight-bearing structure by evolution of an ischium, a full mesio-ventral contact between the two sides of the girdle, an ilium, and a contact between the vertebral column and the girdle through a sacral rib. Fore- and hindlimbs shifted laterally by reorientation of the glenoid and the acetabulum.[well established][VHOG]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", external_class="VHOG:0000974", ontology="VHOG", source="http://bgee.unil.ch/", source="DOI:10.1038/nature04119 Boisvert CA, The pelvic fin and girdle of Panderichthys and the origin of tetrapod locomotion. Nature (2005)"}
property_value: taxon_notes "In reptiles and in birds, the acetabula are deep sockets." xsd:string {source="WP"}

[Term]
id: UBERON:0001270
name: bony pelvis
namespace: uberon
def: "A ring of bone formed by the sacrum and the first few coccygeal vertebrae as the roof, the pubis and ischia as the floor and the ilia and the acetabular part of the ischia as the walls." [http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/bony+pelvis]
def: "In humans, the ring of bone formed by the sacrum and the first few coccygeal vertebrae as the roof, the pubis and ischia as the floor and the ilia and the acetabular part of the ischia as the walls." [http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/bony+pelvis]
comment: in FMA, this is part of the axial skeletal system. todo: add taxon-specific part of relations connecting sub-structures to this.
