[Term]
id: UBERON:0001284
name: renal column
namespace: uberon
def: "A column of tissue that is histologically identical to tissue found in the renal cortex, but which is located in the medulla between the renal pyramids." [http://anatomy.uams.edu/anatomyhtml/kidney.html]
def: "The renal column (or Bertin column, or column of Bertin) is a medullary extension of the renal cortex in between the renal pyramids. It allows the cortex to be better anchored. Each column consists of lines of blood vessels and urinary tubes and a fibrous material. [WP,unvetted]." [Wikipedia:Renal_column]
