[Term]
id: UBERON:0001300
name: scrotum
namespace: uberon
def: "In some male mammals the scrotum (also referred to as the cod) is a protuberance of skin and muscle containing the testicles. It is an extension of the abdomen, and is located between the penis and anus. In humans and some other mammals, the base of the scrotum becomes covered with pubic hair at puberty. In common speech, the scrotum is often improperly referred to as the testicles, which actually refer to organs encased inside the scrotum. The scrotum is homologous to the labia majora in females. It becomes tight when sexually aroused. [WP,unvetted]." [Wikipedia:Scrotum]
def: "the external sac of skin that encloses the testes. It is an extension of the abdomen, and in placentals is located between the penis and anus." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scrotum, MP:0002669\,ISBN\:0-683-40008-8]
subset: pheno_slim
subset: uberon_slim
