[Term]
id: UBERON:0001305
name: ovarian follicle
namespace: uberon
def: "A spherical aggregation of cells in the ovary that contains a single oocyte[WP,modified]." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ovarian_follicle, http://www.repropedia.org/ovarian-follicle]
def: "Ovarian follicles are the basic units of female reproductive biology, each of which is composed of roughly spherical aggregations of cells found in the ovary. They contain a single oocyte (aka ovum or egg). These structures are periodically initiated to grow and develop, culminating in ovulation of usually a single competent oocyte in humans. These eggs/ova are only developed once every menstrual cycle (e.g. once a month in humans)[WP]." [Wikipedia:Ovarian_follicle]
comment: This class was created automatically from a combination of ontologies
subset: pheno_slim
subset: uberon_slim
subset: vertebrate_core
synonym: "egg follicle" RELATED [ZFA:0001110]
