id: UBERON:0001317
name: internal iliac vein
namespace: uberon
def: "A vein that begins near the upper part of the greater sciatic foramen, passes upward behind and slightly medial to the hypogastric artery and, at the brim of the pelvis, joins with the external iliac to form the common iliac vein. [WP,unvetted]." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internal_iliac_vein]
def: "The internal iliac vein (hypogastric vein) begins near the upper part of the greater sciatic foramen, passes upward behind and slightly medial to the hypogastric artery and, at the brim of the pelvis, joins with the external iliac to form the common iliac vein. [WP,unvetted]." [Wikipedia:Internal_iliac_vein]
