[Term]
id: UBERON:0001368
name: obturator externus
namespace: uberon
def: "An adductor muscle that attaches to the femur and the pelvis. In humans, the obturator externus muscle is a flat, triangular muscle, which covers the outer surface of the anterior wall of the pelvis. It is sometimes considered part of the medial compartment of thigh, and sometimes considered part of the gluteal region. [WP,generalized]." [Wikipedia:Obturator_externus_muscle]
