[Term]
id: UBERON:0001388
name: gastrocnemius
namespace: uberon
def: "A muscle of the shank. In mammals it has two heads[Kardong]. It runs from its two heads just above the knee to the heel, and is involved in standing, walking, running and jumping. Along with the soleus muscle it forms the calf muscle. [WP]." [ISBN10:0073040584, Wikipedia:Gastrocnemius_muscle]
def: "The most superficial muscle of the triceps surae group, in the posterior portion of the lower hindleg." [ISBN10:0073040584, MP:0013188, UBERON:cjm]
