[Term]
id: UBERON:0001395
name: thoraco-acromial artery
namespace: uberon
def: "The thoracoacromial artery (acromiothoracic artery; thoracic axis) is a short trunk, which arises from the forepart of the axillary artery, its origin being generally overlapped by the upper edge of the Pectoralis minor. [WP,unvetted]." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thoraco-acromial_artery]
