namespace: uberon
def: "A sesamoid element that is composed of bone tissue." [http://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165]
def: "Ossicle that develops within bands of dense, regular connective tissue (e.g., tendons and ligaments). Sesamoids are generally located proximate to a bony prominence, over which the dense regular connective tissue wraps, and/or a joint or articulation." [VSAO:0000137, Wikipedia:Sesamoid_bone]
comment: Sesamoids are often endochondral replacement elements and in addition to bone tissue, may also be composed of articular cartilage, fibrocartilage, hyaline cartilage, and calcified cartilage.[VSAO]
