[Term]
id: UBERON:0001611
name: sublingual artery
namespace: uberon
def: "A branch of the lingual artery that supplies the sublingual gland." [UBERON:cjm]
def: "The Sublingual Artery arises at the anterior margin of the Hyoglossus, and runs forward between the Genioglossus and Mylohyoideus to the sublingual gland. It supplies the gland and gives branches to the Mylohyoideus and neighboring muscles, and to the mucous membrane of the mouth and gums. One branch runs behind the alveolar process of the mandible in the substance of the gum to anastomose with a similar artery from the other side; another pierces the Mylohyoideus and anastomoses with the submental branch of the external maxillary artery. [WP,unvetted]." [Wikipedia:Sublingual_artery]
