[Term]
id: UBERON:0001633
name: basilar artery
namespace: uberon
def: "A major artery that supplues the hindbrain and runs along the ventral keel of the hindbrain." [BGEE:ann]
def: "In human anatomy, the basilar artery is one of the arteries that supplies the brain with oxygen-rich blood. The two vertebral arteries and the basilar artery are sometimes together called the vertebrobasilar system, which supplies blood to the posterior part of circle of Willis and anastomoses with blood supplied to the anterior part of the circle of Willis from the carotid arteries. [WP,unvetted]." [Wikipedia:Basilar_artery]
