[Term]
id: UBERON:0001702
name: eyelash
namespace: uberon
def: "An eyelash or simply lash is one of the hairs that grow at the edge of the eyelid. Eyelashes protect the eye from debris and perform some of the same function as whiskers do on a cat or a mouse in the sense that they are sensitive to being touched, thus providing a warning that an object is near the eye (which is then closed reflexively). The greek word for eyelash is \"blepharis\". This word is often used as a root in biological terms" [Wikipedia:Eyelash]
def: "An eyelash or simply lash is one of the hairs that grow at the edge of the eyelid. Eyelashes protect the eye from debris and perform some of the same function as whiskers do on a cat or a mouse in the sense that they are sensitive to being touched, thus providing a warning that an object is near the eye (which is then closed reflexively). The greek word for eyelash is 'blepharis'. This word is often used as a root in biological terms" [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eyelash]
