def: "A horn-like keratin structure covering the dorsal aspect of the terminal phalanges of fingers and toes[WP]." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nail_(anatomy)]
def: "a horn-like keratin structure covering the dorsal aspect of the terminal phalanges of fingers and toes[WP]." [Wikipedia:Nail_(anatomy)]
comment: The nails of humans and the claws are moth are highly similar. Both species have a proximal nail fold, cuticle, nail matrix, nail bed, nail plate, and hyponychium. Distinguishing features are the shape of the nail and the presence of an extended hyponychium in the mouse [PMC3579226]
