[Term]
id: UBERON:0001729
name: oropharynx
namespace: uberon
def: "The Oropharynx (oral part of the pharynx) reaches from the Uvula to the level of the hyoid bone. It opens anteriorly, through the isthmus faucium, into the mouth, while in its lateral wall, between the two palatine arches, is the palatine tonsil. [WP,unvetted]." [Wikipedia:Oropharynx]
def: "the portion of the pharynx that lies between the soft palate and the upper edge of the epiglottis" [MP:0002252\,MGI\:cwg]
