[Term]
id: UBERON:0001735
name: tonsillar ring
namespace: uberon
def: "lymphoid tissue ring located in the pharynx and to the back of the oral cavity. The ring consists of (from superior to inferior): Pharyngeal tonsil (also known as 'adenoids' when infected) Tubal tonsil (where Eustachian tube opens in the nasopharynx) Palatine tonsils (commonly called 'the tonsils' in the vernacular, less commonly termed 'faucial tonsils') Lingual tonsils Some animals, but not humans, have one or two additional tonsils: Soft palate tonsil Paraepiglottic tonsil[WP]." [Wikipedia:Waldeyer's_ring]
def: "the circular lymphoid tissue formed by the lingual, pharyngeal, and facial tonsils" [MP:0002379\,MGI\:cwg]
comment: see also FMA:79771 naso-pharyngeal lymphoid tissue
