[Term]
id: UBERON:0001762
name: nasal concha
namespace: uberon
def: "In anatomy, a nasal concha (or turbinate) is a long, narrow and curled bone shelf (shaped like an elongated sea-shell) which protrudes into the breathing passage of the nose. Turbinate bone refers to any of the scrolled spongy bones of the nasal passages in vertebrates. In humans, the turbinates divide the nasal airway into three groove-like air passages –and are responsible for forcing inhaled air to flow in a steady, regular pattern around the largest possible surface of cilia and climate controlling tissue. [WP,unvetted]." [Wikipedia:Nasal_concha]
def: "the small curved bones that extends horizontally along the lateral wall of the nasal passage" [MP:0002244\,ISBN\:0-683-40008-8]
comment: Note that FMA considers nasal concha and nasal concha of ethmoid bone to be synonymous. We disambiguate these here // Turbinals are only ossified in birds and derived synapsids.
subset: pheno_slim
