[Term]
id: UBERON:0001801
name: anterior segment of eyeball
namespace: uberon
def: "any of the parts of the eye that lie in front of, or ventral to, the lens (inclusive)" [MP:0005193\,ISBN\:0-683-40008-8\,MESH\:A09.371.060]
def: "The anterior segment is the front third of the eye that includes the structures in front of the vitreous humour: the cornea, iris, ciliary body, and lens. Within the anterior segment are two fluid-filled spaces: the anterior chamber between the posterior surface of the cornea (i.e. the corneal endothelium) and the iris; the posterior chamber between the iris and the front face of the vitreous. Aqueous humor fills these spaces within the anterior segment and provides nutrients to the surrounding structures." [Wikipedia:Anterior_segment_of_eyeball]
