property_value: homology_notes "One part of the striatum is called the archistriatum. (...) The archistriatum of fishes consists of several indistinctly segregated nuclei called the amygdaloid (...) complex. Tetrapods retain the structure, and in mammals the corresponding amygdala is a globular mass that tends to be ventral to the other basal nuclei.[well established][VHOG]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", external_class="VHOG:0001277", ontology="VHOG", source="http://bgee.unil.ch/", source="ISBN:978-0471090588 Hildebrand M, Analysis of vertebrate structure (1983) p.342"}

[Term]
id: UBERON:0001877
name: medial septal nucleus
namespace: uberon
def: "Cells lying generally in front of Regional_part_of_septal_nuclei, lying ventral to and slightly medial to the lateral septal nucleus. Neurons in this nucleus give rise to the bulk of efferents from the septal nuclei. A major projection from the medial septal nucleus terminates in the hippocampal formation (Adapted from Brodal, 1981)." [NIFSTD:birnlex_1668]
comment: This class was created automatically from a combination of ontologies
synonym: "medial parolfactory nucleus" EXACT [FMA:61879]
