[Term]
id: UBERON:0001903
name: thalamic reticular nucleus
namespace: uberon
def: "The thalamic reticular nucleus is part of the ventral thalamus that forms a capsule around the thalamus laterally. It is separated from the thalamus by the external medullary lamina. Reticular cells are GABAergic, and have discoid dendritic arbors in the plane of the nucleus. Thalamic Reticular Nucleus is variously abbreviated TRN, RTN, NRT, and RT. [WP,unvetted]." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thalamic_reticular_nucleus]
def: "The thalamic reticular nucleus is part of the ventral thalamus that forms a capsule around the thalamus laterally. It is separated from the thalamus by the external medullary lamina. Reticular cells are GABAergic, and have discoid dendritic arbors in the plane of the nucleus. Thalamic Reticular Nucleus is variously abbreviated TRN, RTN, NRT, and RT. [WP,unvetted]." [Wikipedia:Thalamic_reticular_nucleus]
comment: AO notes: only MA considers this part of a subthalamus; MA also considers a subthalamus part of a thalamus
subset: uberon_slim
synonym: "nuclei reticulares (thalami)" RELATED LATIN [NeuroNames:365]
synonym: "nucleus reticularis" RELATED LATIN [NeuroNames:365]
