[Term]
id: UBERON:0001914
name: colostrum
namespace: uberon
def: "The thin, yellow, serous fluid secreted by the mammary glands during pregnancy and immediately postpartum before lactation begins. It consists of immunologically active substances, white blood cells, water, protein, fat, and carbohydrates." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colostrum, MESH:A12.200.194]
def: "The thin, yellow, serous fluid secreted by the mammary glands during pregnancy and immediately postpartum before lactation begins. It consists of immunologically active substances, white blood cells, water, protein, fat, and carbohydrates." [MESH:A12.200.194, Wikipedia:Colostrum]
comment: AO notes: we follow in MA in making this is a sib of mammary gland milk, rather than a subclass.
