id: UBERON:0001944
name: pretectal region
namespace: uberon
def: "Nuclear complex between dorsal thalamus and optic tectum whose nuclei receive afferents primarily from the retina and the optic tectum and are involved in modulating motor behavior in response to visual input." [https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/361, ISBN10:0471888893]
def: "Region between dorsal thalamus and optic tectum[pub]. It receives binocular sensory input from retinal ganglion cells of the eyes, and is the region responsible for maintaining the pupillary light reflex. [WP,unvetted]." [ISBN10:0471888893, Wikipedia:Pretectum]
