namespace: uberon
def: "Large round nucleus located in the midbrain tegmentum, consisting of a magnocellular and parvicellular portion in most species studied." [NIFSTD:birnlex_1478]
def: "The red nucleus is a structure in the rostral midbrain involved in motor coordination. It comprises a caudal magnocellular and a rostral parvocellular part. [WP,unvetted]." [Wikipedia:Red_nucleus]
comment: Function notes: in animals without a significant corticospinal tract, gait is mainly controlled by the red nucleus.
