[Term]
id: UBERON:0001970
name: bile
namespace: uberon
def: "a bitter-tasting, dark green to yellowish brown fluid, produced by the liver of most vertebrates, that aids the process of digestion of lipids in the small intestine. In many species, bile is stored in the gallbladder and upon eating is discharged into the duodenum. Bile is a composition of the following materials: water (85%), bile salts (10%), mucus and pigments (3%), fats (1%), inorganic salts (0.7%) and cholesterol (0.3%)[WP]." [Wikipedia:Bile]
def: "vital aqueous secretion of the liver that is formed by hepatocytes and modified down stream by absorptive and secretory properties of the bile duct epithelium." [http://dx.doi.org/10.1002/cphy.c120027, http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bile]
subset: pheno_slim
subset: uberon_slim
synonym: "fel" RELATED [BTO:0000121]
synonym: "gall" RELATED [BTO:0000121]
