[Term]
id: UBERON:0002250
name: popliteal artery
namespace: uberon
def: "In human anatomy, the popliteal artery is defined as the extension of the 'superficial' femoral artery after passing through the adductor canal and adductor hiatus above the knee. The termination of the popliteal artery is its bifurcation into the anterior tibial artery and posterior tibial artery. The popliteal artery, through numerous smaller branches, supplies blood to the knee joint and muscles in the thigh and calf. It is accompanied, along its length, by the popliteal vein. [WP,unvetted]." [Wikipedia:Popliteal_artery]
def: "The continuation of the femoral artery coursing through the popliteal fossa; it divides into the anterior and posterior tibial arteries." [MESH:A07.231.114.681]
comment: This class was created automatically from a combination of ontologies
