name: nasal mucus
namespace: uberon
def: "In the respiratory system mucus aids in the protection of the lungs by trapping foreign particles that enter it, particularly through the nose, during normal breathing. Phlegm is a specialized term for mucus that is restricted to the respiratory tract, while the term mucus more globally describes secretions of the nasal passages as well." [Wikipedia:Nasal_mucus#Respiratory_system]
