[Term]
id: UBERON:0002331
name: umbilical cord
namespace: uberon
def: "The connecting cord from the developing embryo or fetus to the placenta. During prenatal development, the umbilical cord comes from the same zygote as the fetus and (in humans) normally contains two arteries (the umbilical arteries) and one vein (the umbilical vein), buried within Wharton's jelly. The umbilical vein supplies the fetus with oxygenated, nutrient-rich blood from the placenta. Conversely, the umbilical arteries return the deoxygenated, nutrient-depleted blood[WP]." [Wikipedia:Umbilical_cord]
def: "The connecting cord from the developing embryo to the placenta." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Umbilical_cord\,MP\:0001725\,ISBN\:0-683-40008-8\,PMID\:9144284]
