[Term]
id: UBERON:0002484
name: bone marrow cavity
namespace: uberon
def: "the central cavity of bone shafts where red bone marrow and/or yellow bone marrow (adipose tissue) is stored; hence, the medullary cavity is also known as the marrow cavity. Located in the main shaft (cortical bone) of a long bone (diaphysis) (consisting mostly of compact bone), the medullary cavity has walls composed of spongy bone (cancellous bone) and is lined with a thin, vascular membrane (endosteum)" [Wikipedia:Bone_marrow_of_ovaryry_cavity]
def: "the medullary cavities of the bones where bone marrow is stored" [MP:0000065\,ISBN\:0-683-40008-8\,PMID\:10709991]
comment: AO notes: not clear if the FMA intends to have two classes. MP:0000065: "the medullary cavities of the bones.". NCITA also has "medullary bone"
