[Term]
id: UBERON:0002606
name: neuropil
namespace: uberon
def: "A cluster of neurites that is part of a nervous system and forms a network of dendrites and axons where synapses are present and in which neuronal somata do not occur." [http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/21062451]
def: "A dense intricate feltwork of interwoven fine glial processes, fibrils, synaptic terminals, axons, and dendrites interspersed among the nerve cells of the central nervous system[MESH]" [MESH:A08.637.500, Wikipedia:Neuropil]
subset: uberon_slim
synonym: "neuropilus" RELATED LATIN [Wikipedia:Neuropil]
