[Term]
id: UBERON:0002633
name: motor nucleus of trigeminal nerve
namespace: uberon
def: "Nucleus located in the pontine tegmentum containing cells that give rise to motor innervation of the jaw through the trigeminal nerve.  It receives both crossed and uncrossed fibers from the cerebral cortex (Heimer, L. The Human Brain and Spinal Cord, 2nd ed., 1996, pg 248)." [NIFSTD:birnlex_1222]
def: "The trigeminal motor nucleus contains motor neurons that innervate muscles of the first branchial arch, namely the muscles of mastication, the tensor tympani, tensor veli palatini, mylohyoid, and anterior belly of the digastric." [Wikipedia:Trigeminal_motor_nucleus]
comment: note this in ZFA this is part of the medulla; pons is a dubious structure for zebrafish
