[Term]
id: UBERON:0002640
name: cuneocerebellar tract
namespace: uberon
def: "The posterior external arcuate fibers (dorsal external arcuate fibers) take origin in the gracile and cuneate nuclei; they pass to the inferior peduncle of the same side. It is uncertain whether fibers are continued directly from the gracile and cuneate fasciculi into the inferior peduncle. The term 'cuneocerebellar tract' is sometimes used to collectively refer to the posterior external arcuate fibers. [WP,unvetted]." [Wikipedia:Cuneocerebellar_tract]
def: "White matter tract that originates from the cuneate and external cuneate nuclei.  It relays ascending spinal fibers in the dorsal funiculus and conveys information from forelimbs to the cerebellum." [NIFSTD:birnlex_1238]
subset: uberon_slim
synonym: "cuneocerebellar fibers" EXACT [NIF_GrossAnatomy:birnlex_1238]
synonym: "cuneocerebellar fibers" EXACT [NIFSTD:birnlex_1238]
synonym: "tractus cuneocerebelli" RELATED LATIN [NeuroNames:803]
