[Term]
id: UBERON:0003011
name: facial motor nucleus
namespace: uberon
def: "Nucleus located in the pontine tegmentum containing motor neurons that innervate the muscles of the face.  Some neurons that project to the cerebellum have also been identified in some species." [NIFSTD:birnlex_903]
def: "The facial motor nucleus is a collection of neurons in the brainstem that belong to the facial nerve. These lower motor neurons innervate the muscles of facial expression and the stapedius. [WP,unvetted]." [Wikipedia:Facial_motor_nucleus]
