[Term]
id: UBERON:0003049
name: collagen and cuticulin-based cuticle
namespace: uberon
alt_id: UBERON:WBbt_0005755
def: "A rigid external coating which is secreted by the hypodermis, seam and some transitional epithelial cells which covers the outer body, the major openings into the body cavity from the exterior, and two large sensory bristles, the male spicules. The cuticle of the spicules, the hook, and of some portions of the spicule channels is especially rigid and is probably sclerotized. Similar sclerotic features are occasionally noted in the ventral surface of the male tail fan[WBbt]. The main structural components of the nematode cuticle are proteins, highly cross-linked collagens and specialised insoluble proteins known as cuticlins, together with glycoproteins and lipids[WP]." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165, WA:dh]
comment: Note that GO has a superclass protein-based cuticle development // taxonomic restriction may be too strict
comment: taxonomic restriction may be too strict
subset: uberon_slim
synonym: "nematode cuticle" RELATED []
xref: WBbt:0005755
is_a: UBERON:0001002 ! cuticle
relationship: only_in_taxon NCBITaxon:6231 ! Nematoda
property_value: external_ontology_notes "GO has a superclass protein-based cuticle development" xsd:string {external_ontology="GO"}

