property_value: external_definition "Meninges that are part of the midbrain. [Bgee_curator][VHOG]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", external_class="VHOG:0000012", ontology="VHOG", source="http://bgee.unil.ch/"}
property_value: homology_notes "In fishes, the meninges consist of a single membrane, the primitive meninx, wrapped around the brain and spinal cord. With the adoption of terrestrial life, the meninges doubled. In amphibians, reptiles, and birds, the meninges include a thick outer dura mater derived from mesoderm and a thin inner secondary meninx. (...) In mammals, the dura mater persists, but division of the secondary meninx yields both the arachnoid and the pia mater from ectomesoderm.[well established][VHOG]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", external_class="VHOG:0000012", ontology="VHOG", source="http://bgee.unil.ch/", source="ISBN:978-0072528305 Kardong KV, Vertebrates: Comparative Anatomy, Function, Evolution (2006) p.639"}

