[Term]
id: UBERON:0003713
name: splenic vein
namespace: uberon
def: "A vein arising from the splenic trabecular vein in the hilum of the spleen that drains into the portal vein." [ncithesaurus:Splenic_Vein]
def: "In anatomy, the splenic vein (in the past called the lienal vein) is the blood vessel that drains blood from the spleen. It joins with the superior mesenteric vein, to form the hepatic portal vein and follows a course superior to the pancreas, alongside of the similarly named artery, the splenic artery. It collects branches from the stomach and pancreas and most notably from the large intestine, which is drained by the inferior mesenteric vein and joins with splenic vein shortly before it forms the portal vein. [WP,unvetted]." [Wikipedia:Splenic_vein]
