[Term]
id: UBERON:0003721
name: lingual nerve
namespace: uberon
def: "The lingual nerve is a branch of the mandibular nerve (CN V3), itself a branch of the trigeminal nerve, which supplies sensory innervation to the tongue. It also carries fibers from the facial nerve, which return taste information from the anterior two thirds of the tongue." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lingual_nerve\,Wikipedia\:Lingual_nerve]
