[Term]
id: UBERON:0003957
name: Bruch's membrane
namespace: uberon
def: "A transparent, nearly structureless innermost layer of the choroid in contact with the pigmented layer of the retina." [MP:0005239]
def: "A transparent, nearly structureless innermost layer of the choroid in contact with the pigmented layer of the retina. Bruch's membrane consists of five layers (from inside to outside): 1. the basement membrane of the retinal pigment epithelium; 2. the inner collagenous zone; 3. a central band of elastic fibers; 4. the outer collagenous zone; 5. the basement membrane of the choriocapillaris. The retinal pigment epithelium transports metabolic waste from the photoreceptors across Bruch's membrane to the choroid." [MP:0005239, Wikipedia:Bruch's_membrane]
comment: TODO - see also
