[Term]
id: UBERON:0004031
name: ectomesenchyme
namespace: uberon
def: "mesenchymal cells derived from neural crest cells that contribute to development of the hard and soft tissue in the head and neck, including the branchial arches[MP]." [MP:0006302, Wikipedia:Ectomesenchyme]
def: "mesenchymal cells derived from neural crest cells that contribute to development of the hard and soft tissue in the head and neck, including the branchial arches[MP]." [MP:0006302]
subset: pheno_slim
xref: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ectomesenchyme
xref: Wikipedia:Ectomesenchyme
is_a: UBERON:0005253 ! head mesenchyme
is_a: UBERON:0007213 ! mesenchyme derived from head neural crest
is_a: UBERON:0010313 ! neural crest-derived structure
relationship: develops_from UBERON:0002342 ! neural crest
property_value: external_definition "Ectomesenchyme has similar properties to mesenchyme. The major difference is that ectomesenchyme is usually considered to arise from neural crest cells, which are a critical group of cells that form in the cranial region during early vertebrate development. Thus, ectomesenchyme plays a critical role in the formation of the hard and soft tissues of the head and neck such as bones, muscles, teeth, and, most important, the branchial arches[Wikipedia:Ectomesenchyme]." xsd:string {source="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ectomesenchyme"}
property_value: external_definition "Portion of tissue that develops from the cranial neural crest and which cells populate a series of pharyngeal arches from which develops the support skeleton of the jaw and gills[ZFA:0005771]." xsd:string {source="ZFA:0005771"}

