[Term]
id: UBERON:0004152
name: bulbus arteriosus
namespace: uberon
def: "The bulbus arteriosus is an elastic heart chamber[GO]. Multi-tissue structure that consists of three layers and through which the blood exits the heart. The bulbus arteriosus is a pear shaped chamber that functions as a capacitor, maintaining continuous blood flow into the gill arches[ZFA]." [GO:0003232, http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/15108157]
def: "The bulbus arteriosus is an elastic heart chamber[GO]. Multi-tissue structure that consists of three layers and through which the blood exits the heart. The bulbus arteriosus is a pear shaped chamber that functions as a capacitor, maintaining continuous blood flow into the gill arches[ZFA]." [GO:0003232, PMID:15108157]
comment: Evolution notes: replaces conus arteriosis in cartilaginous fish
