[Term]
id: UBERON:0004164
name: branchiomeric muscle
namespace: uberon
def: "A jaw muscle that arises from cranial mesenchyme and is innervated by cranial nerves." [ISBN10:0073040584]
def: "The branchiomeric muscle is derived from cranial mesoderm and controls facial expression, pharyngeal and laryngeal function, operating the jaw. Branchiomeric muscles of mammals correspond to the gill musculature of fish[GO]." [GO:0014707, Wikipedia:Branchiomeric_musculature]
comment: Note: Kardong uses this term in a different way, including trapezius and mastoid groups
