[Term]
id: UBERON:0004369
name: Reichert's membrane
namespace: uberon
def: "An nonvascular extraembryonic basement membrane that forms on the inner surface of the trophectoderm during placenta morphogenesis and is secreted by the distal parietal endoderm; required for the maternofetal exchange of nutrients and is important for the postgastrulation development[MP]. a thick multilayered basement membrane between the parietal endoderm cells and the trophoblast cells" [DOI:10.1007/BF00184752, MP:0003954]
def: "An nonvascular extraembryonic basement membrane that forms on the inner surface of the trophectoderm during placenta morphogenesis and is secreted by the distal parietal endoderm; required for the maternofetal exchange of nutrients and is important for the postgastrulation development[MP]. a thick multilayered basement membrane between the parietal endoderm cells and the trophoblast cells" [http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/BF00184752, MP:0003954]
subset: pheno_slim
xref: EMAPA:16057
