[Term]
id: UBERON:0004637
name: otic capsule
namespace: uberon
def: "The capsule surrounding the inner ear mechanism." [http://www.biology-online.org/dictionary/Otic_capsule]
def: "The capsule surrounding the inner ear mechanism; in elasmobranchs, it remains cartilaginous in the adult; in the embryos of higher vertebrates, it is cartilaginous at first but later becomes bony (at approximately 23 weeks in humans)[Biology-Online]. Bilaterally paired cartilage encasing the semicircular canals of the inner ear[ZFA]." [http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/otic+capsule, http://www.biology-online.org/dictionary/Otic_capsule, ZFA:0001500]
comment: Taxon notes: developmental relationships need to be checked
synonym: "auditory capsule" RELATED [VHOG:0000854]
synonym: "otic capsule" EXACT [ZFA:0001500]
synonym: "otic capsule element" EXACT [UBERON:endochondral]
synonym: "otic capsule endochondral element" EXACT [UBERON:endochondral]
synonym: "otic capsule skeletal element" BROAD [UBERON:endochondral]
synonym: "otic region" RELATED []
synonym: "periotic" RELATED []
synonym: "periotic capsule" RELATED [VHOG:0000854]
