namespace: uberon
def: "the thin epithelial membrane lining the ventricular system of the brain and the spinal cord. Ependyma is one of the four types of neuroglia in the central nervous system. It is involved in the production of cerebrospinal fluid (CSF). It is simple, columnar or cuboidal." [BTO:0000401, Wikipedia:Ependyma]
def: "The thin epithelium-like membrane composed of ependymal cells that lines the ventricular system of the brain and the spinal cord." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ependyma, ISBN-10:0387949542, UBERON:cjm]
