[Term]
id: UBERON:0004741
name: cleithrum
namespace: uberon
def: "Dermal bone on the margin of the scapula. The cleithrum is attached to the skull in fishes, but free from the latter in amphibians and disappears early in the evolution of reptiles." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cleithrum, VSAO:0000187]
def: "Dermal bone on the margin of the scapula. The cleithrum is attached to the skull in fishes, but free from the latter in amphibians and disappears early in the evolution of reptiles." [VSAO:0000187, Wikipedia:Cleithrum]
comment: Taxon notes: Found in some early members of Chelonia (e.g. Triassochelys), but missing in all later forms.[VSAO]
