relationship: part_of UBERON:0015238 ! pineal complex

[Term]
id: UBERON:0004870
name: superficial cervical lymph node
namespace: uberon
def: "A group of nodes lying along the external jugular vein; they drain the skin and superficial structures over the region of the sternocleidomastoid muscle and anterior cervical regions. Efferent vessels drain to the deep cervical lymph nodes. Lymph nodes can be further subdivided into anterior and lateral groupings." [CL:tm, http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superficial_cervical_lymph_nodes, ref:Stedmans]
def: "A group of nodes lying along the external jugular vein; they drain the skin and superficial structures over the region of the sternocleidomastoid muscle and anterior cervical regions. Efferent vessels drain to the deep cervical lymph nodes. Lymph nodes can be further subdivided into anterior and lateral groupings." [CL:tm, ref:Stedmans, Wikipedia:Superficial_cervical_lymph_nodes]
