name: primary nerve cord
namespace: uberon
def: "A cluster of neurons that is the most prominent longitudinally extending condensed part of a nervous system." [http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/21062451]
comment: Usage notes: some species have multiple longitudinal nerve cords; this class refers to the most prominent one, which is dorsal in chordates and ventral in others.
subset: dubious_grouping
synonym: "nerve cord" EXACT [BILA:0000136]
synonym: "true nerve cord" EXACT [UBERON:cjm]
