[Term]
id: UBERON:0005215
name: kidney interstitium
namespace: uberon
def: "The interstitial compartment of the kidney, comprising the extravascular intertubular spaces of the renal parenchyma, with their attendant cellular elements and extracellular substances, bounded on all sides by epithelial and vascular basement membranes." [http://dx.doi.org/10.1038/ki.1991.49, http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/18575881, UBERON:cjm]
def: "The interstitium of the kidney comprises the extravascular intertubular spaces of the renal parenchyma, with their attendant cellular elements and extracellular substances. As we define it here, the interstitium is bounded on all sides by tubular and vascular basement membranes." [doi:10.1038/ki.1991.49]
subset: pheno_slim
synonym: "interstitial tissue of kidney" EXACT []
