[Term]
id: UBERON:0005333
name: mammary bud
namespace: uberon
alt_id: UBERON:0004181
def: "A bulb of epithelial cells that forms from the mammary placode that develops into the mammary gland." [UBERON:cjm]
def: "Mammary gland buds form by an outpocketing of the mammary placodes and grow to invade the mammary fat, when they form the mammary cord[GO]. produced along the length of the embryonic mammary ridge these buds represent the future locations of the mammary glands. Invagination of ectoderm at each bud leads to the development of epithelial diverticula, later maturing as lactiferous ducts[TFD]." [GO:0060648, http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/mammary+bud]
