property_value: external_definition "It may also refer to the putamen and caudate collectively." xsd:string {source="Dorsal:striatum"}
property_value: external_definition "The term dorsal striatum refers to a composite structure of the endbrain that is defined in the striatopallidal system by connectivity and neurochemical staining. It includes most of the striatum ( Heimer-1995 ). The boundary between this structure and the ventral striatum is indistinct in sections stained for Nissl substance." xsd:string {source="http://braininfo.rprc.washington.edu/centraldirectory.aspx?ID=2340"}

[Term]
id: UBERON:0005383
name: caudate-putamen
namespace: uberon
def: "Regional part of telencephalon in some species, e.g., rodent, equivalent to the dorsal striatum (caudate nucleus and putamen). Unlike the dorsal striatum of primates, for example, the caudoputamen is not split into separate nuclei by the fibers of the internal capsule. Rather, the internal capsule splits into fiber bundles which course through the structure." [NIF_GrossAnatomy:nlx_anat_100312]
def: "Regional part of telencephalon in some species, e.g., rodent, equivalent to the dorsal striatum (caudate nucleus and putamen). Unlike the dorsal striatum of primates, for example, the caudoputamen is not split into separate nuclei by the fibers of the internal capsule. Rather, the internal capsule splits into fiber bundles which course through the structure." [NIFSTD:nlx_anat_100312]
comment: CHECK - rodents. The caudate nucleus and putamen are separated by a clear white matter bundle in most species but not in rodents (MM)
