[Term]
id: UBERON:0005402
name: philtrum
namespace: uberon
def: "medial cleft extending from the nose to the upper lip" [Wikipedia:Philtrum]
def: "the vertical groove found on the median line of the upper lip, extending to the nose" [MP:0012256\,MGI\:anna\,Wikipedia\:Philtrum]
comment: Taxon notes: vestigial in humans. n humans, the philtrum is formed where the nasomedial and maxillary processes meet during embryonic development (colloquially known as Hulse lines). When these processes fail to fuse fully in humans, a cleft lip (sometimes called a 'hare lip') can result. A flattened or smooth philtrum can be a symptom of fetal alcohol syndrome or Prader-Willi syndrome
