[Term]
id: UBERON:0005408
name: circumventricular organ
namespace: uberon
def: "Any of any of the secretory or sensory organs located in the brain region around or in relation to the ventricular system that are characterized by extensive vasculature and a lack of a normal blood brain barrier (BBB) and allow for the linkage between the central nervous system and peripheral blood flow." [MP:0013562]
def: "Brain region located around or in relation to the ventricular system that is highly vascularized and distinguished by the lack of a blood brain barrier." [NIF_GrossAnatomy:nlx_anat_20090312, Wikipedia:Circumventricular_organs]
comment: AO notes: MA subdivides into sensory and secretory
subset: pheno_slim
synonym: "circumventricular organ" EXACT [NIFSTD:nlx_anat_20090312]
synonym: "circumventricular organ" EXACT [NIF_GrossAnatomy:nlx_anat_20090312]
synonym: "circumventricular organ of neuraxis" EXACT [FMA:84081]
synonym: "CVO" EXACT ABBREVIATION [NIFSTD:nlx_anat_20090312]
synonym: "CVO" EXACT [NIF_GrossAnatomy:nlx_anat_20090312]
