[Term]
id: UBERON:0005438
name: coronary sinus
namespace: uberon
def: "The coronary sinus is a collection of veins joined together to form a large vessel that collects blood from the myocardium of the heart. It is present in humans and other animals. The coronary sinus opens into the right atrium, between the inferior vena cava and the auriculo-ventricular opening. It returns the blood from the substance of the heart, and is protected by a semicircular fold of the lining membrane of the auricle, the coronary valve. (valve of Thebesius). The sinus, before entering the auricle, is considerably dilated - nearly to the size of the end of the little finger. Its wall is partly muscular, and at its junction with the great coronary vein is somewhat constricted and furnished with a valve consisting of two unequal segments. - Gray 462" [Wikipedia:Coronary_sinus]
def: "the short trunk that recieves most of the cardiac veins carrying the blood from the myocardium and delivers it to the right atrium, with the sinoatrial connection occurring between the inferior vena cava and the atrioventricular orifice" [MP:0010436\,ISBN\:0-683-40008-8]
subset: pheno_slim
synonym: "sinus coronarius" EXACT []
synonym: "sinus coronarius" RELATED LATIN [Wikipedia:Coronary_sinus]
synonym: "sinus coronarius" RELATED LATIN [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coronary_sinus]
