id: UBERON:0005479
name: superior mesenteric ganglion
namespace: uberon
def: "In the upper part of the superior mesenteric plexus close to the origin of the superior mesenteric artery is a ganglion, the superior mesenteric ganglion. The superior mesenteric ganglion is the synapsing point for one of the pre- and post-synaptic nerves of the sympathetic division of the autonomous nervous system. This nerve goes on to innervate part of the large intestine." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superior_mesenteric_ganglion]
