[Term]
id: UBERON:0005925
name: ethmoidal process of inferior nasal concha
namespace: uberon
def: "Behind the lacrimal process of the inferior nasal conchae lies a broad, thin plate, the ethmoidal process, which ascends to join the uncinate process of the ethmoid; from its lower border a thin lamina, the maxillary process, curves downward and lateralward; it articulates with the maxilla and forms a part of the medial wall of the maxillary sinus." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethmoid_boneal_process_of_inferior_nasal_concha]
def: "Behind the lacrimal process of the inferior nasal conchae lies a broad, thin plate, the ethmoidal process, which ascends to join the uncinate process of the ethmoid; from its lower border a thin lamina, the maxillary process, curves downward and lateralward; it articulates with the maxilla and forms a part of the medial wall of the maxillary sinus." [Wikipedia:Ethmoid_boneal_process_of_inferior_nasal_concha]
