property_value: external_definition "Region of the vertebral column posterior to the caudal-sacral region, that may consists of two or three to more than 100 vertebrae. These vertebrae exhibit a gradual reduction in the sizes of their transverse processes and zygapophyses, but these structures are never entirely absent. All caudal vertebrae bear haemal arches.[AAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-06-20", external_class="AAO:0000082", ontology="AAO", source="AAO:Duellman_and_Trueb_1994"}
