[Term]
id: UBERON:0006081
name: fundus of gallbladder
namespace: uberon
def: "The fundus of gallbladder is the portion of the gallbladder which lies the farthest from the cystic duct. It is covered with peritoneum. A traditional cholecystectomy is most commonly performed from the infundibulum to the fundus. It's at the same level as the transpyloric plane." [Wikipedia:Fundus_of_gallbladder]
def: "The fundus of gallbladder is the portion of the gallbladder which lies the farthest from the cystic duct. It is covered with peritoneum. A traditional cholecystectomy is most commonly performed from the infundibulum to the fundus. It's at the same level as the transpyloric plane." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fundus_of_gallbladder]
