[Term]
id: UBERON:0006216
name: cervical sinus
name: cervical sinus of His
namespace: uberon
def: "A temporary depression caudal to the second pharyngeal arch, containing the succeeding pharyngeal arches; it is overgrown by the second pharyngeal arch and closes off as the cervical vesicle. This sinus is bounded in front by the hyoid arch, and behind by the thoracic wall." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cervical_sinus, http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/cervical+sinus]
def: "a temporary depression caudal to the second pharyngeal arch, containing the succeeding pharyngeal arches; it is overgrown by the second pharyngeal arch and closes off as the cervical vesicle[TFD]." [http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/cervical+sinus, Wikipedia:Cervical_sinus]
comment: This sinus is bounded in front by the hyoid arch, and behind by the thoracic wall; it is ultimately obliterated by the fusion of its walls.
