[Term]
id: UBERON:0006322
name: inferior rectus extraocular muscle
namespace: uberon
def: "A muscle in the orbit that depresses, adducts, and helps extort (rotate laterally) the eye. The inferior rectus muscle is the only muscle that is capable of depressing the pupil when it is in a fully abducted position." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inferior_rectus_muscle]
def: "a muscle in the orbit that depresses, adducts, and helps extort (rotate laterally) the eye. The inferior rectus muscle is the only muscle that is capable of depressing the pupil when it is in a fully abducted position." [Wikipedia:Inferior_rectus_muscle]
