property_value: taxon_notes "In harbor seals, the structure of the vibrissal shaft is undulated (wavy) and flattened. This specialization is also found in most true seals. In contrast, the whiskers of the California sea lion are circular or elliptical in cross-section and are smooth." xsd:string {source="Species_differences_in_vibrissae"}

