[Term]
id: UBERON:0006505
name: palmar hand interosseus muscle
name: palmar interosseous muscle of manus
namespace: uberon
def: "Any of three muscles, the first with its origin from the second metacarpal, and the second and the third with origin from the fourth and fifth metacarpals; the first with insertion into the index finger, and the second and the third with insertion into the ring and little fingers; with nerve supply from the ulnar nerve, and whose action adducts the fingers toward the axis of the middle finger." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palmar_interossei_muscles]
def: "The palmar interossei (interossei volares) are small muscles in the hand that lie on the anterior aspect of the metacarpals. They are smaller than the dorsal interossei of the hand, which lie between the metacarpals" [Wikipedia:Palmar_interossei_muscles]
synonym: "musculi interossei palmares" EXACT []
