[Term]
id: UBERON:0006659
name: cruciate ligament of knee
namespace: uberon
def: "One of a pair of ligaments arranged like a letter X.[1] They occur in several joints of the body, such as the knee. In a fashion similar to the cords in a toy Jacob's ladder, the crossed ligaments stabilize the joint while allowing a very large range of motion[WP]." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cruciate_ligament]
