namespace: uberon
def: "A gap between bones in the skull at the junction of the sagittal suture and lambdoidal suture." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Posterior_fontanelle]
def: "In humans, the posterior fontanelle (or occipital fontanelle) is a gap between bones in the skull, triangular in form and situated at the junction of the sagittal suture and lambdoidal suture. It generally closes in 6–8 weeks from birth. A delay in closure is associated with congential hypothyroidism." [Wikipedia:Posterior_fontanelle]
