[Term]
id: UBERON:0007106
name: chorionic villus
namespace: uberon
def: "One of the minute vascular projections of the fetal chorion that combines with maternal uterine tissue to form the placenta." [BTO:0001161, http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chorionic_villi]
def: "One of the minute vascular projections of the fetal chorion that combines with maternal uterine tissue to form the placenta." [BTO:0001161, Wikipedia:Chorionic_villi]
comment: Taxon notes: The mouse and human placentas have labyrinthine and villous types of interdigitation between maternal and fetal tissues, respectively. Histology notes: The bulk of the villi consist of connective tissues in which blood vessels are found. Most of the cells in the connective tissue core of the villi are fibroblasts. Macrophages known as Hofbauer cells are also present.
