[Term]
id: UBERON:0007162
name: lateral arcuate ligament
namespace: uberon
def: "The lateral arcuate ligament (also lateral lumbocostal arch) is a ligament under the diaphragm that arches across the upper part of the quadratus lumborum. It is traversed by the subcostal nerve, artery and vein." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lateral_arcuate_ligament]
