property_value: homology_notes "Found in all vertebrates, the VP (visceral pericardium) is also known as the cardiac epimysium. This outermost layer of the epicardium consists of a thin layer of mesothelial cells over a dense network of collagen and elastin fibers.[well established][VHOG]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", external_class="VHOG:0000778", ontology="VHOG", source="http://bgee.unil.ch/", source="DOI:10.1152/ajpheart.00967.2007 Jöbsis PD, Ashikaga H, Wen H, Rothstein EC, Horvath KA, McVeigh ER, Balaban RS, The visceral pericardium: macromolecular structure and contribution to passive mechanical properties of the left ventricle. American journal of physiology, Heart and circulatory physiology (2007)"}

