[Term]
id: UBERON:0007250
name: lingual tonsil
namespace: uberon
def: "The lingual tonsils are rounded masses of lymphatic tissue that cover the posterior region of the tongue. They are on the dorsal surface at the base of the tongue. Their lymphatic tissue are dense and nodular, their surface is covered with stratified squamous epithelium which invaginates as a single crypt into each lingual tonsil. They are partially surrounded by connective tissue placing them in the group of Partially-Encapsulated Lymphatic Organs, tonsils, the only one of its kind. They have associated mucous glands which are drained by ducts directly into the single tonsillar crypt." [Wikipedia:Lingual_tonsils]
def: "the lymph tissue on the floor of the oropharyngeal passage, near the root of the tongue" [MP:0002385\,MGI\:cwg]
subset: pheno_slim
synonym: "lingual tonsillar tissue" EXACT [MA:0000773]
synonym: "tonsilla lingualis" RELATED LATIN [Wikipedia:Lingual_tonsils]
synonym: "tonsilla lingualis" RELATED LATIN [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lingual_tonsils]
