[Term]
id: UBERON:0007679
name: intersegmental vein
name: intersomitic vein
namespace: uberon
def: "a vein receiving blood from adjacent bronchopulmonary segments; it emerges from the inferior margin of a segment to become a tributary of a branch of a pulmonary vein[web]. Primary intersegmental vessels that are contacted by secondary angiogenic sprouts from the posterior cardinal vein and take on the characteristics of veins.  These eventually link with other secondary sprouts from the posterior cardinal vein to form the parachordal vessel[ZFA]." [http://www.medilexicon.com/medicaldictionary.php?t=97310, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-030908-4]
def: "The vein that sprouts from the posterior cardinal vein, growing dorsally between the somites, and then joining, and draining the dorsal longitudinal anastomosing vessel." [MGI:anna]
