[Term]
id: UBERON:0007722
name: interphalangeal joint of manus
namespace: uberon
def: "The interphalangeal articulations of hand are hinge-joints of the phalanges of the hand. There are two sets (except in the thumb): \"proximal interphalangeal joints\" (PIP), those between the first (also called proximal) and second (intermediate) phalanges \"distal interphalangeal joints\" (DIP), those between the second and third (distal) phalanges A similar group of articulations also function in the toes." [Wikipedia:Interphalangeal_articulations_of_the_hand]
def: "The interphalangeal articulations of hand are hinge-joints of the phalanges of the hand. There are two sets (except in the thumb): 'proximal interphalangeal joints' (PIP), those between the first (also called proximal) and second (intermediate) phalanges 'distal interphalangeal joints' (DIP), those between the second and third (distal) phalanges A similar group of articulations also function in the toes." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interphalangeal_articulations_of_the_hand]
comment: Editor notes: consider renaming: 'finger' is ambiguous as the term in some usages excludes the thumb (we include it)
subset: pheno_slim
synonym: "articulationes digitorum manus" EXACT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interphalangeal_articulations_of_the_hand]
synonym: "articulationes digitorum manus" EXACT [Wikipedia:Interphalangeal_articulations_of_the_hand]
