[Term]
id: UBERON:0007822
name: vomeronasal cartilage
namespace: uberon
def: "The vomeronasal cartilage (or Jacobson's cartilage) is a narrow strip of cartilage, low on the medial wall of the nasal cavity. It lies between the cartilaginous nasal septum and the vomer. The cartilage lies below, but is not connected to, the rudimentary vomeronasal organ of Jacobson[WP]." [Wikipedia:Vomeronasal_cartilage]
def: "The vomeronasal cartilage (or Jacobson's cartilage) is a narrow strip of cartilage, low on the medial wall of the nasal cavity. It lies between the cartilaginous nasal septum and the vomer. The cartilage lies below, but is not connected to, the rudimentary vomeronasal organ of Jacobson[WP]." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vomeronasal_cartilage]
