[Term]
id: UBERON:0008199
name: chin
namespace: uberon
def: "A subdivision of the face that is the anteriormost part of the lower jaw region." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chin, TAO:0002254]
def: "Surface structure that is the anteriormost part of the lower jaw region. In humans, the chin is the lowermost part of the face. It is formed by the lower front of the mandible. People show a wide variety of chin structures. See Cleft chin. The chin developed as a point of muscular attachment facilitating minute movements of the lips associated with speech. In human evolution, the chin is a cladistic apomorphy, partially defining anatomically modern Humans as distinct from archaic forms." [TAO:0002254, Wikipedia:Chin]
