id: UBERON:0008595
name: levator anguli oris
namespace: uberon
def: "The levator anguli oris (caninus) is a facial muscle of the mouth arising from the canine fossa, immediately below the infraorbital foramen. Its fibers are inserted into the angle of the mouth, intermingling with those of the Zygomaticus, Triangularis, and Orbicularis oris." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Levator_anguli_oris_muscle]
