[Term]
id: UBERON:0008811
name: intromittent organ
namespace: uberon
def: "An external organ of a male organism that is specialized to deliver sperm during copulation. Intromittent organs are found most often in terrestrial species, as most aquatic species fertilize their eggs externally, although there are exceptions[WP]." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intromittent_organ]
def: "an external organ of a male organism that is specialized to deliver sperm during copulation. Intromittent organs are found most often in terrestrial species, as most aquatic species fertilize their eggs externally, although there are exceptions[WP]." [Wikipedia:Intromittent_organ]
