property_value: external_ontology_notes "FMA and MP disagree as to whether the circular layer is middle or innermost" xsd:string {external_ontology="FMA"}
property_value: function_notes "This layer wraps in a circular orientation around the pylorus, and is held in a constricted state normally. The normal constriction of this muscle is what creates the pyloric sphincter, which controls the movement of chyme into the duodenum. This layer is concentric to the longitudinal axis of the stomach. (note: chyme is a thick and acidic mixture of acidic digestive fluids and partially digested food, which moves from the stomach to the small intestine as digestion moves along the digestive tract.) " xsd:string

