[Term]
id: UBERON:0008881
name: rostral migratory stream
namespace: uberon
def: "Unique telencephalic subventricular zones that extend from the lateral ventricles into the olfactory bulbs. Newly produced GABAergic interneurons migrate along the RMS and settle in the bulb." [http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/12453055, NIFSTD:birnlex_1702]
def: "Unique telencephalic subventricular zones that extend from the lateral ventricles into the olfactory bulbs. Newly produced GABAergic interneurons migrate along the RMS and settle in the bulb[NIF]. In rodents, the anterior region of the SVZ produces neuroblasts that migrate in chain toward the olfactory bulb along the so-called rostral migratory stream (RMS)[BTO]. the transient structure formed by neurons migrating from the subventricular zone into the olfactory bulbs[MP] The rostral migratory stream (RMS) or rostral migratory pathway is a pathway, found in the brain of some animals, along which neuronal precursors that originated in the subventricular zone (SVZ) of the brain migrate to reach the main olfactory bulb, where they differentiate into interneurons. Neurogenesis has been shown to occur in the SVZ into adulthood[WP]" [\[Wikipedia:Rostral_migratory_stream, MP:0004279, NIF_GrossAnatomy:birnlex_1702, PMID:12453055]
subset: pheno_slim
synonym: "RMS" RELATED ABBREVIATION [BTO:0003412]
synonym: "rostral migratory pathway" RELATED [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rostral_migratory_stream]
synonym: "rostral migratory pathway" RELATED [Wikipedia:Rostral_migratory_stream]
xref: birnlex:1702
xref: BTO:0003412
xref: DHBA:10556
xref: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rostral_migratory_stream
xref: NIF_GrossAnatomy:birnlex_1702
xref: PBA:128012584
xref: Wikipedia:Rostral_migratory_stream
is_a: UBERON:0002616 ! regional part of brain
is_a: UBERON:0002791 ! obsolete regional part of telencephalon
is_a: UBERON:0010314 ! structure with developmental contribution from neural crest
relationship: connects UBERON:0002264 ! olfactory bulb
relationship: connects UBERON:0002264 ! olfactory bulb
