def: "The lateral ganglia of a snail nervous system are called parietal ganglia. They innerve pallial cavity, gills and skin." [BTO:0001841]
xref: BTO:0001841
is_a: UBERON:0000045 ! ganglion
relationship: only_in_taxon NCBITaxon:6447 ! Mollusca
relationship: part_of UBERON:0008937 ! visceral hump

[Term]
id: UBERON:0008941
name: pleural ganglion
namespace: uberon
def: "A knot of nerves in The pallial cavity that innervates the mantle of a snail[BTO,modified]." [BTO:0001842]
def: "The pallial cavity's nerve knots are called pleural ganglia. They innerve primarily the mantle or a snail." [BTO:0001842]
xref: BTO:0001842
is_a: UBERON:0000045 ! ganglion
relationship: only_in_taxon NCBITaxon:6447 ! Mollusca
relationship: part_of UBERON:0008937 ! visceral hump
