[Term]
id: UBERON:0008967
name: centrum semiovale
namespace: uberon
def: "The semioval center is the white matter found underneath the grey matter on the surface of the cerebrum. The term is synonymous with cerebral white matter. The white matter, located in each hemisphere between the cerebral cortex and nuclei, as a whole has a semioval shape. It consists of cortical projection fibers, association fibers and cortical fibers." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semioval_center]
def: "The semioval center is the white matter found underneath the grey matter on the surface of the cerebrum. The term is synonymous with cerebral white matter. The white matter, located in each hemisphere between the cerebral cortex and nuclei, as a whole has a semioval shape. It consists of cortical projection fibers, association fibers and cortical fibers." [Wikipedia:Semioval_center]
comment: note that WP suggests a merge with cerebral white matter
