[Term]
id: UBERON:0008993
name: habenular nucleus
namespace: uberon
def: "Either of the two neural nuclei within the habenula." [UBERON:cjm]
def: "The gray matter of the habenula, composed of a small-celled medial and a larger-celled lateral habenular nucleus; both nuclei receive fibres from basal forebrain regions (septum, basal nucleus, lateral preoptic nucleus); the lateral habenular nucleus receives an additional projection from the medial segment of the globus pallidus. Both nuclei project by way of the retroflex fasciculus to the interpeduncular nucleus and a medial zone of the midbrain tegmentum." [BTO:0003685]
