[Term]
id: UBERON:0010078
name: optic choroid vascular plexus
namespace: uberon
alt_id: ZFA:0005228
comment: Editor notes: Consider merging with capillary layer. See https://sourceforge.net/tracker/?group_id=76834&atid=1127722. Consider choriocapillaris complex
synonym: "capillary lamina of choroid" RELATED [XAO:0004176]
synonym: "choriocapillaris" RELATED [XAO:0004176]
synonym: "choroid vascular plexus" RELATED []
synonym: "choroid vasculature" RELATED [ZFA:0005094]
synonym: "choroidal vascular plexus" RELATED [TAO:0005094]
synonym: "CVP" EXACT ABBREVIATION [ZFA:0005094]
synonym: "optic choroid vascular plexus" RELATED [XAO:0004176]
xref: TAO:0005094
xref: XAO:0004176
xref: ZFA:0005094
is_a: UBERON:0002203 ! vasculature of eye
is_a: UBERON:0005629 ! vascular plexus
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001776 ! optic choroid
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002200 ! vasculature of head
property_value: editor_note "Consider merging with capillary layer. Consider choriocapillaris complex" xsd:string
property_value: external_definition "A plexus of capillaries that is located anteromedial to the eye. It is a capillary layer in the choroid. It is in contact with the basal surface of the retinal pigmented epithelium and supplies the photoreceptors with oxygen and nutrients. The fused basement membrane of this capillary layer and the pigmented epithelium is called Bruch's membrane.[XAO:0004176]." xsd:string {source="XAO:0004176"}
property_value: external_definition "A plexus of capillaries that is visible anteromedial to the eye. The choroid is the vascular layer of the eye, containing connective tissue, and lying between the retina and the sclera. The choroid provides oxygen and nourishment to the outer layers of the retina. Along with the ciliary body and iris, the choroid forms the uveal tract[XAO:0004176]." xsd:string
property_value: external_definition "Is an ocular vasculature that develops adjacent to the pigment epithelium of the eye. The optic choroid vascular plexus develops from the primitive mesencephalic artery. Initially blood enters from the mesencephalic central artery, and the dorsal ciliary vein. The plexus drains via the ophthalmic vein. The plexus supplies blood to the retina[ZFA:0005094]." xsd:string {source="ZFA:0005094"}
property_value: taxon_notes "The choroid of teleosts is a connective tissue layer rich in blood vessels, and one or two choroidal glands." xsd:string {source="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/14738502"}

