[Term]
id: UBERON:0010292
name: episcleral layer of eyeball
namespace: uberon
def: "The episclera is the outermost layer of the sclera. It is composed of loose, fibrous, elastic tissue and attaches to Tenon's capsule. A vascular plexus is found between the conjunctiva and the sclera consisting of two layers of vessels, the superficial episcleral vessels and the deep episcleral vessels." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Episcleral_layer]
def: "The episclera is the outermost layer of the sclera. It is composed of loose, fibrous, elastic tissue and attaches to Tenon's capsule. A vascular plexus is found between the conjunctiva and the sclera consisting of two layers of vessels, the superficial episcleral vessels and the deep episcleral vessels." [Wikipedia:Episcleral_layer]
