[Term]
id: UBERON:0010306
name: bulbar conjunctiva
namespace: uberon
def: "The part of the conjunctiva, a thin transparent mucous membrane, that is loosely attached the orbital septum and covers the anterior surface of the sclera." [ncithesaurus:Bulbar_Conjunctiva]
comment: covers the eyeball, over the sclera. This region of the conjunctiva is tightly bound to the underlying sclera by Tenon's capsule and moves with the eyeball movements.
subset: pheno_slim
synonym: "ocular conjunctiva" EXACT [Wikipedia:Conjunctiva]
