[Term]
id: UBERON:0010308
name: os opticus
namespace: uberon
def: "Scleral element located at the posterior pole of the scleral cartilage surrounding the foramen through which the optic nerve fibers pass. the internal architecture of this bone reveals a cancellous marrow cavity with fatty tissue." [PMID:16496288]
def: "Scleral element located at the posterior pole of the scleral cartilage surrounding the foramen through which the optic nerve fibers pass. the internal architecture of this bone reveals a cancellous marrow cavity with fatty tissue." [http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/16496288]
comment: Taxon notes: At present, it has been documented in 219 species from 35 families, including perching birds, woodpeckers, hummingbirds, toucans, kingfishers, and falcons (Tiemeier, 1950). Morphologically, this element varies in shape from a complete encircling element in some woodpeckers (e.g., Melanerpes eryth- rocephalus) to an abbreviated arc in Gallus
synonym: "Gemminger's ossicle" EXACT [PMID:16496288]
synonym: "Gemminger's ossicle" EXACT [http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/16496288]
synonym: "os nervi optici" EXACT [http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/16496288]
synonym: "os nervi optici" EXACT [PMID:16496288]
is_a: UBERON:0010298 ! intramembranous scleral ossicle
property_value: taxon_notes "At present, it has been documented in 219 species from 35 families, including perching birds, woodpeckers, hummingbirds, toucans, kingfishers, and falcons (Tiemeier, 1950). Morphologically, this element varies in shape from a complete encircling element in some woodpeckers (e.g., Melanerpes eryth- rocephalus) to an abbreviated arc in Gallus" xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0010309
name: palpebral bone
namespace: uberon
def: "An ossified element investing the upper eyelid." [PMID:16496288, Wikipedia:Palpebral_(bone)]
def: "An ossified element investing the upper eyelid." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palpebral_(bone), http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/16496288]
comment: Taxon notes: The most extreme development of the palpebral is found in the armored dino- saur Euoplocephalus tutus, where the bone forms a quarter-sphere and adducts to completely occlude the or- bit (Coombs, 1972; Vickaryous and Russell, 2003). Notwithstanding the superficially similar position, palpe- brals and tarsal plates differ both anatomically and developmentally and are not considered homologous (Gauthier et al., 1988). Editor notes PMID:16496288 says 'invests' the eyelid, is this consistent across taxa?
synonym: "palpebral" EXACT []
xref: Palpebral:(bone)
xref: Wikipedia:Palpebral_(bone)
