[Term]
id: UBERON:0010368
name: pulmonary lobule
namespace: uberon
def: "The smallest anatomical unit of the lung, measuring 0.50 to 2.00 cm in diameter. Each lobule is composed of 4-8 terminal bronchioles and their distal alveolar ducts and sacs. The lobules are separated by fibrous interlobular septa." [ncithesaurus:Pulmonary_Lobule]
xref: FMA:75739
