is_a: UBERON:0008907 ! dermal bone
relationship: adjacent_to UBERON:0000209 ! tetrapod frontal bone
relationship: adjacent_to UBERON:0001680 ! lacrimal bone
relationship: dubious_for_taxon NCBITaxon:9606 ! Homo sapiens
relationship: foaf-depicted_by http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/44/Dromaeosaurus_skull_en.svg
relationship: only_in_taxon NCBITaxon:8287 ! Sarcopterygii
relationship: overlaps UBERON:0001697 ! orbital region
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003113 ! dermatocranium
relationship: part_of UBERON:0011156 ! facial skeleton
property_value: taxon_notes "It first evolved in the sarcopterygian clade Rhipidistia, which includes lungfish and the Tetrapodomorpha. The prefrontal is found in most modern and extinct lungfish, amphibians and reptiles. It is very small, fused to the frontals or lost in many groups of coelurosaurian theropod dinosaurs and is completely absent in their modern descendants, the birds. The prefrontal was also lost in early mammaliaforms and so is not present in modern mammals either" xsd:string {source="WP"}

