[Term]
id: UBERON:0010856
name: patagium
namespace: uberon
def: "A membranous extension of skin that forms the wing material in animals such as bats. It typically comprises a number of patagial segments, stretching from the side of the body between the forelimb digits and sometimes the hindlimbs." [http://animals.about.com/od/zoologytermsktoz/g/patagium.htm, http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patagium, http://www.brown.edu/Departments/EEB/EML/background/wing_anatomy.htm]
def: "A membranous extension of skin that forms the wing material in animals such as bats. It typically comprises a number of patagial segments, stretching from the side of the body between the forelimb digits and sometimes the hindlimbs." [http://animals.about.com/od/zoologytermsktoz/g/patagium.htm, http://www.brown.edu/Departments/EEB/EML/background/wing_anatomy.htm, Wikipedia:Patagium]
