[Term]
id: UBERON:0010904
name: pectoral fin scapula
namespace: uberon
def: "Endochondral bone that is located medial to the cleithrum, and articulates ventrally with the coracoid, medially with the mesocoracoid when the later is present and posteriorly with the upper one to three proximal radials. The scapula develops from the scapulocoracoid cartilage and belongs to the primary pectoral girdle. It may be perforated by the scapular foramen or it may be notched ventrally and forms together with a similar notch of the coracoid the scapulocoracoid foramen." [TAO:0000583]
comment: Alternate definition: A scapula that is connected to a pectoral fin
synonym: "hypercoracocïde@fr" EXACT [TAO:0000583]
