[Term]
id: UBERON:0010933
name: orbicularis oris muscle
namespace: uberon
def: "In human anatomy, the orbicularis oris muscle is the sphincter muscle around the mouth. This muscle closes the mouth and puckers the lips when it contracts." [Wikipedia:Orbicularis_oris_muscle]
def: "The orbicularis oris is a superficial facial muscle with fibers that encircle the opening of the oral cavity that attaches to the maxilla, mandible, skin and modiolus, and that participates in oral/pharyngeal behaviors, and is innervated by the facial nerve (CN VII)." [FEED:rd, http://dx.doi.org/ 10.1111/j.1469-7580.2009.01111.x, http://dx.doi.org/10.1002/ar.21355, http://www.feedexp.org/wiki/Mammalian_Muscle_Ontology_Workshop, MFMO:0000058]
