[Term]
id: UBERON:0011169
name: postorbital bone
namespace: uberon
def: "The postorbital is one of the bones in vertebrate skulls which forms a portion of the dermal skull roof and, sometimes, a ring about the orbit. Generally, it is located behind the postfrontal and posteriorly to the orbital fenestra. In some vertebrates, the postorbital is fused with the postfrontal to create a postorbitofrontal." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Postorbital_bone]
def: "The postorbital is one of the bones in vertebrate skulls which forms a portion of the dermal skull roof and, sometimes, a ring about the orbit. Generally, it is located behind the postfrontal and posteriorly to the orbital fenestra. In some vertebrates, the postorbital is fused with the postfrontal to create a postorbitofrontal." [Wikipedia:Postorbital_bone]
synonym: "postorbital" BROAD []
