[Term]
id: UBERON:0011199
name: prostatic utricle
namespace: uberon
def: "a small indentation located in the prostatic urethra, at the apex of the urethral crest, on the seminal colliculus (verumontanum), laterally flanked by openings of the ejaculatory ducts. It is also known as the vagina masculina or (in older literature) vesicula prostatica. It is often described as \"blind,\" meaning that it is a duct that does not lead to any other structures. It can sometimes be enlarged." [Wikipedia:Prostatic_utricle]
def: "A small indentation located in the prostatic urethra, at the apex of the urethral crest, on the seminal colliculus (verumontanum), laterally flanked by openings of the ejaculatory ducts. It is also known as the vagina masculina or (in older literature) vesicula prostatica. It is often described as 'blind,' meaning that it is a duct that does not lead to any other structures. It can sometimes be enlarged." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prostatic_utricle]
