[Term]
id: UBERON:0011221
name: ora serrata of retina
namespace: uberon
def: "The ora serrata is the serrated junction between the retina and the ciliary body. This junction marks the transition from the simple non-photosensitive area of the retina to the complex, multi-layered photosensitive region. In animals in which the region does not have a serrated appearance, it is called the ora ciliaris retinae." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ora_serrata]
def: "The ora serrata is the serrated junction between the retina and the ciliary body. This junction marks the transition from the simple non-photosensitive area of the retina to the complex, multi-layered photosensitive region. In animals in which the region does not have a serrated appearance, it is called the ora ciliaris retinae." [Wikipedia:Ora_serrata]
