is_a: UBERON:0004119 ! endoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from UBERON:0007026 ! presumptive gut
relationship: existence_starts_during UBERON:0000068 ! embryo stage
relationship: existence_starts_during UBERON:0000068 ! embryo stage
property_value: structure_notes "Their walls are composed primarily of epithelial cells, but ciliated and glandular cells are also present." xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0011289
name: pharyngobasilar fascia
namespace: uberon
def: "The pharyngeal aponeurosis (or pharyngobasilar fascia, or fibrous coat), is situated between the mucous and muscular layers. It is thick above where the muscular fibers are wanting, and is firmly connected to the basilar portion of the occipital and the petrous portions of the temporal bones. As it descends it diminishes in thickness, and is gradually lost. It is strengthened posteriorly by a strong fibrous band, which is attached above to the pharyngeal spine on the under surface of the basilar portion of the occipital bone, and passes downward, forming a median raphe, which gives attachment to the Constrictores pharyngis." [Wikipedia:Pharyngobasilar_fascia]
def: "The pharyngeal aponeurosis (or pharyngobasilar fascia, or fibrous coat), is situated between the mucous and muscular layers. It is thick above where the muscular fibers are wanting, and is firmly connected to the basilar portion of the occipital and the petrous portions of the temporal bones. As it descends it diminishes in thickness, and is gradually lost. It is strengthened posteriorly by a strong fibrous band, which is attached above to the pharyngeal spine on the under surface of the basilar portion of the occipital bone, and passes downward, forming a median raphe, which gives attachment to the Constrictores pharyngis." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pharyngobasilar_fascia]
synonym: "pharyngeal aponeurosis" EXACT [FMA:55074]
synonym: "pharyngeal aponeurosis" RELATED [Wikipedia:Pharyngobasilar_fascia]
