[Term]
id: UBERON:0011379
name: male external urethral sphincter
namespace: uberon
def: "The external sphincter muscle of urethra (or sphincter urethrae membranaceae) surrounds the whole length of the membranous portion of the urethra, and is enclosed in the fasciæ of the urogenital diaphragm. They arch across the front of the urethra and bulbourethral glands, pass around the urethra, and behind it unite with the muscle of the opposite side, by means of a tendinous raphé." [Wikipedia:External_sphincter_muscle_of_male_urethra]
def: "The external sphincter muscle of urethra (or sphincter urethrae membranaceae) surrounds the whole length of the membranous portion of the urethra, and is enclosed in the fasciæ of the urogenital diaphragm. They arch across the front of the urethra and bulbourethral glands, pass around the urethra, and behind it unite with the muscle of the opposite side, by means of a tendinous raphé." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/External_sphincter_muscle_of_male_urethra]
comment: AO notes: MA includes a term bulboglandular - some sources claim this as the muscles that are associated with the bulbourethral gland, so we place this here
synonym: "bulboglandular" RELATED [MA:0002273]
