[Term]
id: UBERON:0011677
name: trunk vertebra
namespace: uberon
def: "A vertebra in the trunk region. For tetrapods, includes lumbar and thoracic vertebrae. Excludes caudal/coccygeal vertebra, which are located posteriorly. In tetrapods this includes thoracic, lumbar and sacral vertebrae, and excludes the cervical vertebrae, which are located anteriorly." [UBERONREF:0000006]
def: "A vertebra in the trunk region. For tetrapods, includes lumbar and thoracic vertebrae. Excludes cervical, caudal, sacral (if present)." [UBERONREF:0000006]
subset: pheno_slim
synonym: "abdominal vertebra" RELATED [TAO:0000263]
synonym: "abdominal vertebrae" RELATED [TAO:0000263]
synonym: "precaudal vertebra" RELATED [TAO:0000263]
synonym: "precaudal vertebrae" RELATED PLURAL [TAO:0000263]
synonym: "presacral vertebra" RELATED [UBERON:cjm]
synonym: "thoracolumbar vertebra" EXACT []
synonym: "trunk vertebra" RELATED [TAO:0000263]
synonym: "trunk vertebrae" RELATED [TAO:0000263]
xref: TAO:0000263
xref: ZFA:0000263
is_a: UBERON:0003463 ! trunk bone
is_a: UBERON:0004247 ! bone of dorsum
is_a: UBERON:0004451 ! trunk or cervical vertebra
intersection_of: UBERON:0002412 ! vertebra
intersection_of: part_of UBERON:0009568 ! trunk region of vertebral column
relationship: fma_set_term FMA:72066
relationship: part_of UBERON:0009568 ! trunk region of vertebral column
property_value: external_definition "Post-Weberian vertebrae lacking hemal spines (Weitzman, 1962), refers generally to the anterior vertebral region bounding the abdominal cavity.  Alternate but not quite synonymous terms are abdominal or trunk vertebrae, which bear parapophyses and ribs. In many actinopterygians dorsal to the posterior abdominal cavity there are transitional vertebrae lacking ribs but also without hemal spines or sometimes even enclosed hemal arches. The primary definition would identify these vertebrae as precaudal. Bird and Mabee, 2003.[TAO]" xsd:string
property_value: external_definition "Post-Weberian vertebrae lacking hemal spines (Weitzman, 1962), refers generally to the anterior vertebral region bounding the abdominal cavity. Alternate but not quite synonymous terms are abdominal or trunk vertebrae, which bear parapophyses and ribs. In many actinopterygians dorsal to the posterior abdominal cavity there are transitional vertebrae lacking ribs but also without hemal spines or sometimes even enclosed hemal arches. The primary definition would identify these vertebrae as precaudal. Bird and Mabee, 2003.[TAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-08-14", external_class="TAO:0000263", ontology="TAO", source="ZFIN:curator"}
property_value: external_ontology_notes "in TAO this is defined as post-Weberian, this may not precisely align with the definition of being part of the trunk" xsd:string {external_ontology="TAO"}

