[Term]
id: UBERON:0012294
name: navicular fossa of spongiose part of urethra
namespace: uberon
def: "The dilated terminal portion of the male spongy urethra located in the glans penis right before the external urethral orifice, also referred to as the most distal pendulous urethra; it is lined by stratified squamous, non-keratinizing epithelium; during development, the glans of the penis is initially solid but cannulates to give rise to the navicular fossa." [MP:0011838, MP:anna, Wikipedia:Navicular_fossa_of_male_urethra]
def: "The dilated terminal portion of the male spongy urethra located in the glans penis right before the external urethral orifice, also referred to as the most distal pendulous urethra; it is lined by stratified squamous, non-keratinizing epithelium; during development, the glans of the penis is initially solid but cannulates to give rise to the navicular fossa." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Navicular_fossa_of_male_urethra, MP:0011838, MP:anna]
