property_value: external_definition "Anatomical cluster that is the upper roof of the mouth that is underlain by bones such as the parasphenoid, vomer, metapterygoid, orbitosphenoid.[TAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-08-14", external_class="TAO:0002093", ontology="TAO", source="TAO:wd"}
property_value: external_definition "Roof of the mouth lined with ciliated epithelium.[AAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-06-20", external_class="AAO:0010535", ontology="AAO", source="AAO:BJB"}
property_value: homology_notes "Early tetrapod possessed a primary palate that included the vomer, pterygoid, parasphenoid, palatine and ectopterygoid bones. Therapsid evolved a partial secondary palate formed by the medial extension of the premaxilla and maxilla. Mammals have a secondary palate that, in addition to extensions of the premaxilla and maxilla, includes part of the palatine bone[VHOG]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-11-28", external_class="VHOG:0000362", ontology="VHOG", source="http://bgee.unil.ch/", source="ISBN:978-0072528305 Kardong"}

