[Term]
id: UBERON:0012450
name: Meisner's corpuscle
name: Meissner's corpuscle
namespace: uberon
def: "A type of nerve ending in the skin that is responsible for sensitivity to light touch. In particular, they have highest sensitivity (lowest threshold) when sensing vibrations lower than 50 Hertz. They are rapidly adaptive receptors." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meissner%27s_corpuscle]
def: "Meissner's corpuscles (or tactile corpuscles) are a type of mechanoreceptor. They are a type of nerve ending in the skin that is responsible for sensitivity to light touch. In particular, they have highest sensitivity (lowest threshold) when sensing vibrations lower than 50 Hertz. They are rapidly adaptive receptors." [Wikipedia:Meissner%27s_corpuscle]
