[Term]
id: UBERON:0013193
name: parakeratinized epithelium
namespace: uberon
def: "An epithelium that is characterized by incomplete keratinization of the cells in the stratum corneum. The cells are flattened and composed primarily of packed tonofilaments. However, the cells may retain remnants of nuclei and other organelles" [http://www.dental.pitt.edu/informatics/periohistology/en/glossary.html]
comment: Example: parts of oral epithelium
comment: found in oral epithelium
is_a: UBERON:0000488 ! atypical epithelium

[Term]
id: UBERON:0013194
name: orthokeratinized epithelium
namespace: uberon
def: "A keratinized epithelium in which the cells of the stratum corneum become very flat, loose their nuclei and cytoplasmic organelles and are now composed of densely packed tonofilaments cemented by filaggrin" [http://www.dental.pitt.edu/informatics/periohistology/en/glossary.html]
is_a: UBERON:0000488 ! atypical epithelium

