is_a: UBERON:0005913 ! zone of bone organ
is_a: UBERON:0010313 ! neural crest-derived structure
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001684 ! mandible

[Term]
id: UBERON:0013454
name: spheno-maxillary fossa
namespace: uberon
def: "The speno-maxillary fossa is a small triangular space situated at the angle of the junction of the spheno-maxillary and pterygo-maxillary fissures, and placed beneath the apex of the orbit. It is formed above by the under surface of the body of the sphenoid and by the orbital process of the palate bone." [Wikipedia:Spheno-maxillary_fossa]
def: "The speno-maxillary fossa is a small triangular space situated at the angle of the junction of the spheno-maxillary and pterygo-maxillary fissures, and placed beneath the apex of the orbit. It is formed above by the under surface of the body of the sphenoid and by the orbital process of the palate bone." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spheno-maxillary_fossa]
