[Term]
id: UBERON:0013511
name: ambiens muscle
namespace: uberon
def: "A long muscle found in reptiles that originates on the ilium and crosses the acetabulum and the knee joint before being inserted on the tibia." [ISBN10:0073040584]
def: "The tendon of the ambiens muscle passes obliquely over the knee joint. It assists in the control of the bird’s toes. This muscle is present in some reptiles but not mammals. It is present in caiques and some other South American genera, but missing in most parrot genera. This was first noted by Garrod (1874) who proposed using this and other anatomical differences to classify parrots.  For other anatomical differences among parrots see carotid arteries, furcula, and uropygial gland. " [http://caiquesite.com/glossary.htm]
synonym: "ambiens" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:0001630 ! muscle organ
is_a: UBERON:0003663 ! hindlimb muscle
relationship: has_muscle_insertion UBERON:0000979 ! tibia
relationship: has_muscle_origin UBERON:0001273 ! ilium
relationship: only_in_taxon NCBITaxon:40674 ! Mammalia
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002103 ! hindlimb
property_value: external_definition "The tendon of the ambiens muscle passes obliquely over the knee joint. It assists in the control of the bird’s toes. This muscle is present in some reptiles but not mammals. It is present in caiques and some other South American genera, but missing in most parrot genera. This was first noted by Garrod (1874) who proposed using this and other anatomical differences to classify parrots. For oproperty_value external_definitionanatomical differences among parrots see carotid arteries, furcula, and uropygial gland" xsd:string {source="http://caiquesite.com/glossary.htm"}

