[Term]
id: UBERON:0013646
name: buccal nerve
namespace: uberon
def: "The buccal nerve (also called the long buccal nerve) is a nerve in the face. It is a branch of the mandibular nerve (which is itself a branch of the trigeminal nerve) and transmits sensory information from skin over the buccal membrane (in general, the cheek) and from the second and third molar teeth." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buccal_nerve]
