is_a: UBERON:0011970 ! talofibular ligament

[Term]
id: UBERON:0013726
name: posterior talofibular ligament
namespace: uberon
def: "The posterior talofibular ligament, runs almost horizontally from the depression at the medial and back part of the fibular malleolus (lateral malleolus) to a prominent tubercle on the posterior surface of the talus immediately lateral to the groove for the tendon of the flexor hallucis longus." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Posterior_talofibular_ligament]
synonym: "ligamentum talofibulare posterius" EXACT LATIN [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Posterior_talofibular_ligament]
xref: FMA:44084
