[Term]
id: UBERON:0014446
name: acetabular notch
namespace: uberon
def: "The acetabulum presents below a deep notch, the acetabular notch, which is continuous with a circular non-articular depression, the acetabular fossa, at the bottom of the cavity: this depression is perforated by numerous apertures, and lodges a mass of fat. The notch is converted into a foramen by the transverse ligament; through the foramen nutrient vessels and nerves enter the joint; the margins of the notch serve for the attachment of the ligament of the head of the femur." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acetabular_notch]
xref: Acetabular:notch
xref: FMA:16944
xref: http://www.snomedbrowser.com/Codes/Details/289767000
