[Term]
id: UBERON:0014770
name: palpebral artery
namespace: uberon
def: "An artery that supplies blood to an eyelid." [http://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165]
xref: http://www.snomedbrowser.com/Codes/Details/148571007
is_a: UBERON:0001637 ! artery
is_a: UBERON:0003496 ! head blood vessel
intersection_of: UBERON:0001637 ! artery
intersection_of: supplies UBERON:0001711 ! eyelid
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000033 ! head
relationship: supplies UBERON:0001711 ! eyelid
property_value: taxon_notes "In humans, the eyelids are supplied with blood by two arches on each upper and lower lid. The arches are formed by anastamoses of the lateral palpebral arteries and medial palpebral arteries, branching off from the lacrimal artery and ophthalmic artery, respectively. In amphibians, the eyelids may be supplied by branches of the lateral pretrosal arteries.[cjm]" xsd:string

