xref: http://linkedlifedata.com/resource/umls/id/C2697661
xref: http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Ileocecocolic_Lymph_Node
xref: http://www.snomedbrowser.com/Codes/Details/29180003
xref: MA:0003065
is_a: UBERON:0000029 ! lymph node
property_value: editor_note "Can be subclassed based on position relative to terminal branches of the vessel. Consider adding subclasses for these: (a) ileal, in relation to the ileal branch of the artery;(b) anterior ileocolic, usually of three glands, in the ileocolic fold, near the wall of the cecum;(c) posterior ileocolic, mostly placed in the angle between the ileum and the colon, but partly lying behind the cecum at its junction with the ascending colon;(d) a single gland, between the layers of the mesenteriole of the vermiform process;(e) right colic, along the medial side of the ascending colon." xsd:string
property_value: external_definition "A lymph node at the ileocecocolic junction." xsd:string {source="ncithesaurus:Ileocecocolic_Lymph_Node"}

