[Term]
id: UBERON:0016411
name: intergluteal cleft
namespace: uberon
def: "The gluteal sulcus (also known as the gluteal fold or horizontal gluteal crease) is an area of the body of humans and great apes, described by a horizontal crease formed by the inferior aspect of the buttocks and the posterior upper leg. It is one of the major defining features of the buttocks. Children with developmental dysplasia of the hips are born with uneven gluteal folds and can be diagnosed with physical examination and sonogram." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gluteal_sulcus\,Wikipedia\:Gluteal_sulcus]
