id: UBERON:0017621
name: cephalic spine
namespace: uberon
alt_id: UBERONTEMP:8c052198-acff-4165-b1a0-fd6bb2de6e10
def: "One of the spines, probably denticle derivatives, occurring singly or in pairs just behind the orbit on the cheek area in some fossil sharks. May have occurred only in males and may have served to hold the female during copulation, e.g. in the Jurassic genera Hybodus, Asteracanthus and Acrodus." [http://www.briancoad.com/dictionary/complete%20dictionary.htm]
synonym: "cephalic spines" RELATED PLURAL [UBERONTEMP:8c052198-acff-4165-b1a0-fd6bb2de6e10]
