[Term]
id: UBERON:0018389
name: interoceptor
namespace: uberon
def: "A sensory receptor that detects stimulus within the body. Examples of stimuli that would be detected by interoceptors include blood pressure and blood oxygen level." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interoceptor]
synonym: "enteroceptor" EXACT [FMA:84656]
synonym: "visceroceptor" EXACT [FMA:84656]
xref: FMA:84656
xref: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interoceptor
is_a: UBERON:0012451 ! sensory receptor

[Term]
id: UBERON:0018391
name: chemoreceptor
namespace: uberon
def: "A sensory receptor that detects chemical stimulus within the body." [UBERON:cjm]
xref: FMA:85604
xref: MESH:A08.800.550.700.120
is_a: UBERON:0018389 ! interoceptor
property_value: external_definition "Cells specialized to detect chemical substances and relay that information centrally in the nervous system. Chemoreceptors may monitor external stimuli, as in taste and olfaction, or internal stimuli, such as the concentrations of oxygen and carbon dioxide in the blood." xsd:string {source="MESH:A08.800.550.700.120"}

[Term]
