[Term]
id: UBERON:0022272
name: corticobulbar tract
namespace: uberon
def: "The corticobulbar (or corticonuclear) tract is a white matter pathway connecting the cerebral cortex to the brainstem. The term \"bulbar\" refers to the brainstem, as \"bulb\" was a historical term meaning the area currently called the brainstem. The 'bulb' is an archaic term for the medulla oblongata. In clinical usage, it includes the pons as well." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corticobulbar_tract]
synonym: "bulbar" RELATED [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corticobulbar_tract]
