[Term]
id: UBERON:0023984
name: rostral spinocerebellar tract
namespace: uberon
def: "Originates from cells rostral to Clarke's column and sends uncrossed axons through the lateral funiculus to the cerebellum. It reaches the cerebellum partly through the brachium conjunctivum and partly through the restiform body, terminating bilaterally in the anterior lobe of the cerebellum" [NIFSTD:nlx_anat_1010019]
