[Term]
id: UBERON:0024078
name: principal anterior division of supraoptic nucleus
namespace: uberon
def: "One of two divisions of the supraoptic nucleus observed in mammals, formed by the ascension of the optic chiasm to split the nucleus in two. The principal anterior division consists of a dense cluster of large cells that stain darkly in Nissl preparations adjacent to the optic chiasm, extending as far rostrally to the organum vasculosum of the lamina terminalis and caudally into the posterior hypothalamus." [NIFSTD:nlx_anat_20090310]
synonym: "principal anterior division of supraoptic nucleus" EXACT [NIFSTD:nlx_anat_20090310]
xref: nlx_anat:20090310
is_a: UBERON:0002616 ! regional part of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000955 ! brain

[Term]
id: UBERON:0024079
name: tuberal supraoptic nucleus
namespace: uberon
def: "Posterior division of the supraoptic nucleus, formed by the ascension of the optic tract splitting the nucleus into two regions. The tuberal SON lies along the posterior tuber cinereum of the hypothalamus. In some species, some neurons lie under the optic chiasm." [NIFSTD:nlx_anat_20090311]
synonym: "retrochiasmatic subdivision" RELATED [NIFSTD:nlx_anat_20090311]
synonym: "tuberal supraoptic nucleus" EXACT [NIFSTD:nlx_anat_20090311]
xref: nlx_anat:20090311
is_a: UBERON:0006568 ! hypothalamic nucleus
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001929 ! supraoptic nucleus

