xref: http://www.snomedbrowser.com/Codes/Details/362527007
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:0034921 ! multi organ part structure
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001711 ! eyelid

[Term]
id: UBERON:0034773
name: uncus of parahippocampal gyrus
namespace: uberon
def: "The anterior extremity of the Parahippocampal gyrus is recurved in the form of a hook, the uncus, which is separated from the apex of the temporal lobe by a slight fissure, the incisura temporalis. Although superficially continuous with the hippocampal gyrus, the uncus forms morphologically a part of the rhinencephalon. The term uncus was coined by Felix Vicq dbAzyr (1748b1794)." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uncus]
synonym: "pyriform area (Crosby)" RELATED [NeuroNames:40]
synonym: "uncus" RELATED LATIN [NeuroNames:40]
synonym: "uncus hippocampi" EXACT LATIN [NeuroNames:40]
xref: DHBA:12165
xref: FMA:74884
xref: http://braininfo.rprc.washington.edu/centraldirectory.aspx?ID=40
xref: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uncus
xref: http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Uncus
xref: http://www.snomedbrowser.com/Codes/Details/279213004
is_a: UBERON:0002616 ! regional part of brain
is_a: UBERON:0010314 ! structure with developmental contribution from neural crest
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002973 ! parahippocampal gyrus

