[Term]
id: UBERON:0035086
name: plane of autotomy
namespace: uberon
def: "An anatomical plane that bisects a zone of weakness in an appendage. When autotamy occurs, the appendage divides along this plane." [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autotomy, UBERON:cjm]
is_a: UBERON:0035085 ! anatomical plane
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000026 ! appendage
property_value: curator_notes "this class is intended for autotomy that bisects an appendage. Other forms of autotomy are possible: for example, a sea cucumber and autotomitize internal organs" xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0035087
name: fracture plane
namespace: uberon
def: "A plane of autotomy that divides an appendage through a bone." [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autotomy, UBERON:cjm]
synonym: "plane of autotomy bisecting bone" EXACT [UBERON:cjm]
is_a: UBERON:0035086 ! plane of autotomy

[Term]
id: UBERON:0035088
name: vertebral fracture plane
namespace: uberon
def: "A plane of autotomy that divides an appendage through a vertebral bone." [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autotomy, UBERON:cjm]
synonym: "plane of autotomy bisecting vertebral bone" EXACT [UBERON:cjm]
is_a: UBERON:0035087 ! fracture plane
property_value: taxon_notes "Interestingly, zones of cartilage or connective tissue do not demarcate the fracture planes in A. carolinensis, as seen in other lizard taxa (Cox, 1969a; Hoffstetter and Gasc, 1969)[PMID:22753107]" xsd:string
property_value: taxon_notes "Many authors (e.g., Holder, 1960; Mufti and Hafiz, 1972; Bellairs and Bryant, 1985; Russell and Bauer, 1992) have referred to the more proximal caudal vertebrae that lack fracture planes as 'pygal vertebrae' and the more distal caudal vertebrae that possess fracture planes as 'postpygal vertebrae' However, many lizard taxa lack fracture planes in their caudal vertebrae altogether, making this classification difficult to apply in these cases (Etheridge, 1967; Bellairs and Bryant, 1985). Furthermore, in some species (including A. carolinensis) the most distal of the transverse process-bearing vertebrae may possess fracture planes and should technically be called postpygal vertebrae, despite the fact that they more closely resemble the more proximal, non-fracture plane-bearing vertebrae in overall morphology (Cox, 1969a)[PMID:22753107]" xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0035089
name: plane of autotomy bisecting joint
namespace: uberon
def: "A plane of autotomy that divides an appendage in the space between appendage bones." [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autotomy, UBERON:cjm]
is_a: UBERON:0035086 ! plane of autotomy

[Term]
id: UBERON:0035090
name: plane of autotomy bisecting intervertebral joint
namespace: uberon
def: "A plane of autotomy that divides an appendage in the space between vertebrae." [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autotomy, UBERON:cjm]
