[Term]
id: UBERON:0035210
name: paracolic gutter
namespace: uberon
def: "The paracolic gutters (paracolic sulci, paracolic recesses) are spaces between the colon and the abdominal wall. There are two paracolic gutters: The right lateral paracolic gutter. The left lateral paracolic gutter. These gutters are clinically important because they allow a passage for infectious fluids from different compartments of the abdomen. For example; fluid from an infected appendix can track up the right paracolic gutter to the hepatorenal recess." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paracolic_gutters\,Wikipedia\:Paracolic_gutters]
synonym: "paracolic sulcus" EXACT [FMA:14719]
