[Term]
id: UBERON:1000022
name: Zymbal's gland
namespace: uberon
def: "A modified sebaceous glands that are located at the base of the external ear and secrete into the auditory canal" [http://ctrgenpath.net/static/atlas/mousehistology/Windows/senses/zymbalgland.html]
def: "A multilobulated modified sebaceous gland that is located at the base of the external ear, lined by stratified squamous epithelium, and secretes into the auditory canal" [http://ctrgenpath.net/static/atlas/mousehistology/Windows/senses/zymbalgland.html, ISBN10:0123813611, MP:0013384]
comment: Structure notes: Zymbal’s glands are located beneath squamous epithelium at the anterior and posterior aspect of the ear canal, and as a single external gland that is located anterior and ventral to the base of the external ear canal. The bilateral Zymbal’s glands are adjacent to the auditory canal and are made up of several lobules of modified sebaceous glands - http://ratguide.com/health/neoplasia/zymbals_gland_tumor.php. Editor notes: modified sebacious gland or subtype?
synonym: "auditory sebaceous gland" RELATED [ISBN10:0123813611]
synonym: "gland of Zymbal" RELATED []
synonym: "Zymbal gland" RELATED [MA:0002900]
