[Term]
id: UBERON:2000127
name: antorbital
namespace: uberon/phenoscape-anatomy
def: "Dermal bone positioned as the first bone of the infraorbital series. The antorbital articulates with the lacrimal or infraorbital 1 anteroventrally and the supraorbital posterodorsally. The antorbital is a paired bone." [TAO:GA_TG]
comment: The antorbital in some teleosts fuses with the lacrimal. The antorbital contains the end branch of the infraorbital canal or neuromasts for the infraorbital canal in basal teleosts such as elopiformes, some osteoglossomorphs and fossil basal teleosts.
synonym: "adnasal" EXACT [TAO:Goodrich_1930, TAO:Regan_1923]
synonym: "lateral rostral" EXACT [TAO:Jollie_1984]
synonym: "perorbital" EXACT [TAO:Bridge_1877]
