[Term]
id: UBERON:2000691
name: supraorbital bone
namespace: uberon/phenoscape-anatomy
def: "Dermal bone that is part of the dorsal or upper border or antero-dorsal border of the orbit. The supraorbital bone may contact the orbital margin of the frontal bone medially, the antorbital antero-ventrally and the dermosphenotic posteriorly. The supraorbital bone does not carry sensory canals. The supraorbital bone is paired." [TAO:GA_TG]
comment: The supraorbital bone may be present as two or one bone in extant teleosts, although many of the advanced forms lack the bone.
xref: ZFA:0000691
