[Term]
id: UBERON:2001579
name: ural vertebra 2
namespace: uberon/phenoscape-anatomy
def: "Ural vertebra that is the second vertebra posterior to preural centrum 1. It may bear a rudimentary neural arch and sometimes a rudimentary spine or the neural arch and spine are completely absent and it may articulate or fuse with hypural 2 (polyural terminology). Ural vertebra 2 is an unpaired median bone." [TAO:GA_TG]
comment: Ural vertebrae 2 may be defined also as the second ural vertebrae bearing hypurals 3 or 3 and 4 or 3 plus more dorsal hypurals (diural terminology).
xref: ZFA:0001579
