[Term]
id: UBERON:2001998
name: posttemporal-supracleithrum
namespace: uberon/phenoscape-anatomy
def: "Dermal bone that results from the fusion of the dermal posttemporal and the dermal supracleithrum. Forms the upper skeletal element of the pectoral girdle between the cleithrum and neurocranium. Posttemporal-supracleithrum is paired." [TAO:wd]
comment: A posttemporo-supracleithrum is a bone present in Siluriformes. There are different opinions if this is the result of an ontogenetic or a phylogenetic fusion or the loss or one or other bone.
