[Term]
id: UBERON:3000587
name: obsolete supraangular
namespace: uberon/phenoscape-anatomy
def: "The suprangular or surangular is a jaw bone found in most land vertebrates, except mammals. It's usually in the back of the jaw, on the upper edge, and is connected to all other jaw bones: dentary, angular, splenial and articular. It is often a muscle attachment site." []
