[Term]
id: UBERON:4000172
name: lepidotrichium
namespace: uberon/phenoscape-anatomy
def: "Dermal bone that is rod-like, formed and usually contained in a fin membrane, and jointed to or adjacent to distal radials. Lepidotrichia are formed from paired hemitrichia surrounding actinotrichia. There are usually two more lepidotrichia than distal radials." [TAO:curator]
comment: Need to review develops_from relationship to actinotrichia. Lepidotrichia require actinotrichia for development, but develops_from may not be appropriate relationship.  See Zhang et al 2010 for details.  doi:10.1038/nature09137
synonym: "fin ray" BROAD [] {seeAlso="VSAO:0000172"}
