comment: Need to fix the cranial nerve foramena relationships. Some (optic nerve) are currently asserted to be embryonic structures, others (trochlear nerve) are asserted to be anatomical spaces, and some fenestra, which do not link up wiht conduit. Also need to discuss difference between fenestra and foramena. One (fenestra) is a "window" and denotes a large hole or space in a bone. The other (foramen) denotes the passage for a nerve or blood vessel, is restriced in size and may extend to more than one bone.  
is_a: UBERON:0005744 ! cranial conduit
